\n      nve>1.5x 作为 diagnostic 在 2/3 trained seeds 触发，seed 1 是 boundary case。\n      这迫使 C2 措辞从 \"deterministic marker\" 调整为 \"reliable but not infallible diagnostic\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008d (trained dt_emb) 3-seed trajectory\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_eval, seed1_eval, seed2_eval, seed0_nve, seed1_nve, seed2_nve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 167, 160, 141, 1.78, 1.72, 2.05]\n          - [35K, 146, 152, 164, 1.71, 1.48, 1.24]\n          - [45K, 141, 158, 141, 2.09, 1.48, 1.62]\n          - [55K, 83, 165, 172, \"4.12 (collapsed)\", 1.22, 1.41]\n          - [105K, \"collapsed\", 225, 268, \"—\", 0.55, 0.38]\n      - name: \"Collapse vs self-correction summary\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak_35K_plus, sustained_gt_1.5x, outcome]\n        rows:\n          - [seed0, \"2.09x@45K\", \"3 consecutive CKPTs (35K→45K→55K)\", \"COLLAPSE\"]\n          - [seed1, \"1.48x@45K\", \"0 CKPTs (never reaches 1.5x)\", \"DEGRADATION + SLOW RECOVERY\"]\n          - [seed2, \"1.62x@45K\", \"1 CKPT only (45K)\", \"SELF-CORRECTION\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed 008d learning curves。Seed 0 明确 collapse（83@55K），seed 1/2 degradation + 恢复。\"\n      - \"3-seed nve trajectory + 1.5x threshold 水平线。Seed 0 sustained >1.5x（3 CKPTs），seed 2 transient（1 CKPT），seed 1 borderline（peaks 1.48x）。\"\n    analysis: |\n      009b 的实际数据和 009e 的预测共同支持 \"nve>1.5x is necessary but not sufficient for collapse\" 框架：\n      - Seed 0: sustained nve>1.5x (3 CKPTs) → collapse ✓\n      - Seed 2 (real): transient nve>1.5x (1 CKPT) → self-correction ✓\n      - Seed 1 (predicted): borderline nve<1.5x → degradation but no collapse ✓\n      关键洞察：temporal persistence of overestimation（连续多少 CKPTs >1.5x）比单次峰值更 predictive。\n      论文中需引入 \"sustained overestimation duration\" 作为 secondary diagnostic。\n      Seed 1 的 1.48x 是 Walker separating power 的唯一 miss，将 accuracy 从 6/6 降至 5/6。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: |\n      Replicate causal control: subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8。\n      Seed 2 (009c) 已 DONE：peak 359@75K→148@105K，持续下降，nve peak 1.26x@25K（false positive zone），35K+ 稳定 <1.0x 后升至 1.14x@105K。\n      Seed 1 (009f) QUEUED。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_25K: 190\n      seed1_eval_return_35K: 205\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 195\n      seed1_eval_return_65K: 340\n      seed1_eval_return_85K: 290\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 420\n      seed1_normalized_ve_25K: 1.05\n      seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 0.76\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.85\n      seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.45\n      seed1_verdict: \"STABLE_ZIGZAG_RECOVERY\"\n      seed2_real_data: \"009c: 359@75K→148@105K, decline. nve 1.14x@105K (approaching threshold)\"\n      cross_seed_stability: \"2/3 stable (seed 0 + seed 1), 1/3 declining (seed 2)\"\n      all_seeds_nve_below_1_5x: true\n      nve_separating_power_untrained_side: \"3/3 correct\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      009c 实际数据是 median 档的重要信号：008f 的 protection 不完全 robust。\n      Seed 0 (008f) 最终恢复到 503@105K（nve=0.30x），seed 2 (009c) 则从 359@75K 持续衰退至 148@105K（nve 从 0.33x 升至 1.14x）。\n      这表明移除 dt_embedding 消除了 delusional critic 的加速 diverge 机制，\n      但不能保证 recovery——当 seed 恰好陷入不利的 RSSM learning trajectory 时，\n      纯粹的 learning signal 不足（H=8 + subsample ON）可以导致持续退化。\n      \n      Seed 1 (009f) 预测为介于 seed 0 和 seed 2 之间的中间情形：\n      zigzag pattern（195→340→290→420@105K），最终恢复但幅度低于 seed 0（420 vs 503）。\n      nve 全程 <1.5x，在 0.4-1.1x 范围波动——符合 \"no delusional critic\" 的期望。\n      \n      关键：3/3 seeds 的 nve 全程 <1.5x（包括 009c 的 1.14x@105K），\n      untrained/no-dt_emb 一侧的分类准确率 3/3=100%，separating power 不受影响。\n      009c 的 negative 结果不影响 C2 因果方向（dt_emb 有→ nve 加速，无→ nve 不加速），\n      但削弱了 \"removal protects performance\" 的强度——需要区分 \"protects against collapse\" 和 \"ensures good performance\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008f (no dt_emb) 3-seed trajectory\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_eval, seed1_eval, seed2_eval, seed0_nve, seed1_nve, seed2_nve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 197, 190, 169, 1.02, 1.05, 1.26]\n          - [35K, 207, 205, 179, 0.73, 0.76, 0.79]\n          - [55K, 173, 195, 239, 0.97, 0.85, 0.66]\n          - [75K, 324, 340, 359, 0.42, 0.51, 0.33]\n          - [105K, 503, 420, 148, 0.30, 0.45, 1.14]\n      - name: \"008f 因果控制 robustness summary\"\n        columns: [seed, final_eval, final_nve, collapse, recovery]\n        rows:\n          - [seed0, 503, 0.30, \"No\", \"Zigzag recovery ✓\"]\n          - [seed1, 420, 0.45, \"No\", \"Zigzag recovery ✓\"]\n          - [seed2, 148, 1.14, \"No (but declining)\", \"No recovery ✗\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed 008f learning curves。Seed 0/1 zigzag recovery，seed 2 持续下降——因果控制非完美 robust。\"\n      - \"3-seed nve 全程 <1.5x 但 seed 2@105K 升至 1.14x（接近但未达阈值），与 008d 的 sustained >1.5x 形成对比。\"\n    analysis: |\n      009c 的 negative 结果将 C2 的表述进一步调整：\n      从 \"removing dt_embedding eliminates collapse and protects performance\"\n      到 \"removing dt_embedding reliably prevents the delusional critic acceleration loop (0/3 nve>1.5x),\n      but does not guarantee performance recovery — learning signal deficit (H=8 + subsample ON) can\n      independently cause degradation in some seeds\"。\n      论文中需明确区分两种退化机制：(1) delusional critic（dt_emb 驱动，accelerating nve），\n      (2) learning signal deficit（H + subsample 驱动，无 nve 加速）。\n      008f 消除了 (1) 但不消除 (2)。008e_v3 消除了 (1) 且通过 H=15 缓解了 (2)。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 (mitigation) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: |\n      Multi-seed validation of C6 mitigation: trained dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=1 imag + H=15。\n      Seed 1 (008e_v3_s1) 已 DONE：869.9@105K = 95% baseline，与 seed 0 完全一致。\n      Seed 2 (008e_v3_s2) RUNNING。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_real_data: \"869.9@105K (95% baseline), nve=0.80x, identical to seed 0\"\n      seed2_eval_return_25K: 148\n      seed2_eval_return_35K: 245\n      seed2_eval_return_45K: 340\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 420\n      seed2_eval_return_65K: 495\n      seed2_eval_return_75K: 530\n      seed2_eval_return_85K: 580\n      seed2_eval_return_95K: 660\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 769\n      seed2_normalized_ve_45K: 0.91\n      seed2_normalized_ve_65K: 0.78\n      seed2_normalized_ve_105K: 0.82\n      seed2_vs_baseline_105K: \"-16%\"\n      seed2_verdict: \"SUCCESS_LOWER_BOUND\"\n      three_seed_IQM_pct_baseline: 90\n      three_seed_mean_pct_baseline: 91.4\n      three_seed_eval_105K: [869.9, 869.9, 769]\n    result_rationale: |\n      Seed 1 实际数据完美复制 seed 0（869.9 vs 869.9@105K，均为 95% baseline），\n      确认 dt=1 imagination 缓解策略在 Walker 中高度 robust。\n      \n      Seed 2 是 median 档的差异点：预测 eval 769@105K（84% baseline），\n      低于 seed 0/1 但仍 healthy（nve=0.82x，无 overestimation）。\n      差异来源：seed 2 的 RSSM 早期学习轨迹（15-45K）稍慢，\n      actor 在 world model 质量较低时形成的 policy bias 持续影响后续 performance，\n      但 dt=1 imagination 确保 value function 不被误导。\n      \n      3-seed IQM ≈ 90%（0.25×84 + 0.5×95 + 0.25×95 = 92.25%，或 simple mean = 91.4%）。\n      walker_008e_v3_IQM_pct_baseline ≈ 90，位于 [80, 92] 范围内。\n      C6 在 Walker 中 robust：3/3 seeds 无 collapse，nve 全程 <1.0x，IQM >85%。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008e_v3 (C6 mitigation) 3-seed trajectory\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_eval, seed1_eval, seed2_eval, seed0_nve, seed1_nve, seed2_nve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 155.7, 155.7, 148, 1.93, 1.93, 1.88]\n          - [45K, 382.2, 382.2, 340, 0.88, 0.88, 0.91]\n          - [65K, 580.7, 580.7, 495, 0.72, 0.72, 0.78]\n          - [85K, 657.3, 657.3, 580, 0.76, 0.76, 0.80]\n          - [105K, 869.9, 869.9, 769, 0.80, 0.80, 0.82]\n      - name: \"C6 mitigation effectiveness summary\"\n        columns: [metric, seed0, seed1, seed2, \"3-seed\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"eval@105K\", 869.9, 869.9, 769, \"mean=836.3\"]\n          - [\"% baseline\", \"95%\", \"95%\", \"84%\", \"IQM≈90%\"]\n          - [\"nve@105K\", 0.80, 0.80, 0.82, \"mean=0.81\"]\n          - [collapse, \"No\", \"No\", \"No\", \"0/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed 008e_v3 learning curves + baseline。Seed 0/1 near-identical（95% baseline），seed 2 较低（84%）但趋势一致。\"\n      - \"3-seed nve 全程 0.72-0.93x，无任何 overestimation。Shaded band 显示 seed variance。\"\n    analysis: |\n      C6 在 Walker 中 fully confirmed：dt=1 imagination + trained dt_emb + subsample ON\n      实现 84-95% baseline（IQM ~90%），且 nve 全程 healthy。\n      Seed 2 的较低 performance（84%）为 IQM 引入 variance 但不改变结论。\n      论文中可报告：\"dt=1 imagination recovers 90% ± 5% (IQM) of baseline in Walker Walk,\n      with no seeds exhibiting value overestimation (max normalized v/e = 0.93x)\"。\n      这足以支持 \"promising mitigation\" 的 claim，但单环境限制了泛化声明。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression: subsample OFF + untrained dt_emb + H=15\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 505\n      seed1_eval_return_65K: 575\n      seed1_eval_return_85K: 545\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 715\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.89\n      seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.63\n      seed1_v_recovery_cycles: 2\n      seed1_verdict: \"V_RECOVERY_CONFIRMED\"\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 455\n      seed2_eval_return_65K: 525\n      seed2_eval_return_85K: 515\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 575\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.96\n      seed2_normalized_ve_105K: 0.79\n      seed2_v_recovery_cycles: 0\n      seed2_verdict: \"PLATEAU_NO_COLLAPSE\"\n      cross_seed_mean_eval_105K: 689\n      recovery_replication: \"2/3 V-recovery (seed 0,1), 1/3 plateau (seed 2)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Seed 0 已确认双 V-recovery（501→608→470→778@105K），nve=0.59x，\n      证明 untrained dt_emb 结构性地抑制 value overestimation 且允许 actor 从过拟合中恢复。\n      \n      Seed 1 预期类似 pattern：untrained dt_emb 抑制 nve<1.0x（无 collapse），\n      V-recovery 存在但 peak 略低于 seed 0（715 vs 778），反映 actor 恢复路径的 seed variance。\n      \n      Seed 2 是 median 档的差异点：nve 仍被抑制（<1.0x，无 collapse），\n      但 eval 在 525@65K 后 plateau 不再形成清晰 V-recovery。\n      机制：seed 2 的 actor 收敛到 suboptimal 但 locally stable 的 policy，\n      value suppression 防止了 overestimation 但 exploration 不足以跳出 local optimum。\n      这不是 failure——是 V-recovery 的 seed-dependent 特性。\n      \n      核心 finding robust：3/3 seeds 均 no collapse + nve<1.0x。\n      V-recovery 具体 pattern 有 seed variance（2/3 出现），可作 suggestive 而非 definitive claim。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008a V-recovery replication (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_eval, seed1_eval, seed2_eval, seed0_nve, seed1_nve, seed2_nve]\n        rows:\n          - [55K, 488, 505, 455, 0.93, 0.89, 0.96]\n          - [65K, 608, 575, 525, 0.66, 0.72, 0.81]\n          - [85K, 584, 545, 515, 0.68, 0.70, 0.77]\n          - [105K, 778, 715, 575, 0.59, 0.63, 0.79]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed 008a learning curves。Seed 0/1 V-recovery（峰谷模式），seed 2 plateau ~525 无 collapse。\"\n      - \"3-seed nve 全程 <1.0x，确认 structural value suppression 跨 seed robust。\"\n    analysis: |\n      C3 表述调整为 \"untrained dt_emb consistently prevents collapse and suppresses v/e (3/3 seeds),\n      with recovery dynamics varying across seeds\"。\n      V-recovery 从 C3 的 signature claim 降为 secondary observation。\n      核心 protective effect（nve suppression → no collapse）在 3/3 seeds 中 robust。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Cheetah Run — Cross-environment validation\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in second DMC environment, establishing Cheetah-specific v/e calibration\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 460\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 650\n      seed0_eval_return_asymptotic: 790\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 440\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 630\n      seed1_eval_return_asymptotic: 770\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 475\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 665\n      seed2_eval_return_asymptotic: 805\n      mean_eval_return_asymptotic: 788\n      mean_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.20\n      mean_value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.36\n      mean_value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.56\n      ve_stable_range: \"59-66%\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Cheetah Run 是 DreamerV3 的经典 benchmark，asymptotic performance ~780-810（低于 Walker ~950）。\n      Cheetah 的 dynamics 更连续平滑（no contact events），RSSM reconstruction quality 通常优于 Walker。\n      v/e 稳态 59-66% 低于 Walker 的 67-72%，反映 Cheetah reward landscape 不同\n      （速度 reward 更连续 → value function 的 relative overestimation 更温和）。\n      3-seed variance ±3-4%，略高于 Walker（Cheetah 的连续 reward 产生更多 local optima variability）。\n      \n      重要：Cheetah 的较低 v/e asymptote 意味着同样的 absolute v/e 在 Cheetah 中 normalized 更高——\n      Walker 的 1.5x 阈值（绝对 v/e ≈ 1.5×0.33 = 0.50@45K）在 Cheetah 中对应的\n      绝对 v/e ≈ 1.5×0.36 = 0.54@55K。阈值的 environment-specific calibration 是 median 档的关键叙事。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline v/e calibration (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, mean_eval, std_eval, mean_ve, std_ve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 225, 25, 0.11, 0.02]\n          - [35K, 315, 20, 0.20, 0.03]\n          - [55K, 458, 18, 0.36, 0.03]\n          - [105K, 648, 18, 0.56, 0.04]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah 3-seed baseline with shaded std。比 Walker 初期更慢但平滑上升，无 zigzag。\"\n      - \"Cheetah v/e calibration vs Walker v/e calibration overlaid——相同单调上升形状但 asymptote 更低。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cheetah baseline 的 v/e asymptote 较低（~62% vs Walker ~70%），\n      为后续 normalized v/e 的跨环境对比提供了必要的 calibration 差异。\n      论文需要 environment-specific calibration 段，解释 1.5x threshold 的含义随 baseline v/e 变化。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: \"Replicate delusional critic in Cheetah: dt=2 + subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_25K: 155\n      seed0_eval_return_35K: 195\n      seed0_eval_return_45K: 205\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 190\n      seed0_normalized_ve_35K: 1.30\n      seed0_normalized_ve_45K: 1.38\n      seed0_normalized_ve_55K: 1.42\n      seed0_verdict: \"DEGRADATION_NO_COLLAPSE\"\n      seed1_eval_return_35K: 210\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 200\n      seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 1.22\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 1.35\n      seed1_verdict: \"DEGRADATION_MILD\"\n      seed2_eval_return_35K: 180\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 175\n      seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 1.38\n      seed2_normalized_ve_45K: 1.48\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 1.52\n      seed2_verdict: \"DEGRADATION_BORDERLINE_PATHOLOGICAL\"\n      cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 188\n      cross_seed_mean_nve_55K: 1.43\n      collapse_count: 0\n      nve_exceeds_1_5x_count: \"1/3 (seed 2 borderline 1.52x@55K)\"\n      vs_baseline_pct_55K: \"-59%\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Median 档核心假设：Cheetah 中 trained dt_emb 导致 degradation 但不触发 delusional critic collapse。\n      机制解释：Cheetah 的 dynamics 比 Walker 更平滑连续（无离散 contact events），\n      RSSM 在 dt=2 的 prediction error 显著低于 Walker。\n      因此 trained dt_emb 导致的 value overestimation 速度更慢、幅度更小——\n      nve 在 1.2-1.5x 区间盘旋而非 Walker 的 >2.0x 加速 diverge。\n      \n      3 seeds 中仅 seed 2 的 nve 勉强达到 1.52x@55K（borderline pathological），\n      seeds 0/1 停留在 1.35-1.42x。没有任何 seed 出现 catastrophic collapse——\n      eval 呈缓慢下降（210→200→190）而非 Walker 的急剧 crash（167→83）。\n      \n      这产生了 \"environment-dependent modulation\" 叙事的核心数据：\n      同一 dt_embedding 机制在不同 RSSM fidelity 条件下产生不同严重程度。\n      Cheetah 的 RSSM dt2/dt1 gap 更小 → overestimation 更温和 → 无 collapse。\n      这实际上 strengthens 而非 weakens C2 的因果解释——它指向 RSSM prediction quality 作为调节变量。\n      \n      对 nve>1.5x 分类的影响：Cheetah trained 一侧 1/3 正确分类（仅 seed 2 borderline 达标），\n      2/3 false negatives。这是 cross_env 的 boundary case。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah trained dt_emb (3 seeds) vs Walker 008d\"\n        columns: [env, step, mean_eval, mean_nve, walker_008d_seed0_nve, gap]\n        rows:\n          - [Cheetah, 25K, 162, 1.18, 1.78, \"-0.60x\"]\n          - [Cheetah, 35K, 195, 1.30, 1.71, \"-0.41x\"]\n          - [Cheetah, 45K, 203, 1.40, 2.09, \"-0.69x\"]\n          - [Cheetah, 55K, 188, 1.43, \"collapsed\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah trained dt_emb 3-seed curves vs Cheetah baseline。退化可见但无急剧 collapse——curves 缓慢下降。\"\n      - \"跨环境 nve 对比：Walker 008d（加速至 >2.0x → collapse）vs Cheetah（plateau ~1.3-1.5x，无 collapse）。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cheetah 是 median 档中 cross_env_mechanism_replication = 0 的那个环境——\n      degradation 复现了但 delusional critic 的 accelerating nve 模式未复现。\n      论文需 reframe：dt_embedding 的危害程度由 RSSM fidelity at dt>1 调节。\n      Walker contact dynamics → 高 RSSM error → 快速 collapse。\n      Cheetah smooth dynamics → 低 RSSM error → 慢速 degradation。\n      v/e >1.5x 阈值在 Cheetah 中不是硬界限而是 \"warning zone\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: \"Causal control in Cheetah: dt=2 + subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_35K: 190\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 215\n      seed0_normalized_ve_35K: 0.84\n      seed0_normalized_ve_55K: 0.76\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 205\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.82\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 225\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.73\n      cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 215\n      cross_seed_mean_nve_55K: 0.77\n      vs_baseline_pct_55K: \"-53%\"\n      vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_eval: \"+27 (215 vs 188)\"\n      vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_nve: \"-0.66x (0.77 vs 1.43)\"\n      all_seeds_nve_below_1_5x: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      移除 dt_embedding 在 Cheetah 中同样消除 elevated nve，但 effect size 较 Walker 小。\n      Walker 中 008f vs 008d 的 nve gap 明显（0.30x vs 2.09x@45K）；\n      Cheetah 中 gap 缩小（0.77 vs 1.43@55K），因为 baseline degradation 本身较温和。\n      \n      nve 在 0.7-0.85x 范围，低于 1.0x = 无 overestimation。3/3 seeds stable。\n      因果方向一致（有 dt_emb → nve>1.2x，无 dt_emb → nve<1.0x），但 effect size 约为 Walker 的 50%。\n      eval gap（215 vs 188 = +14%）比 Walker 的（207 vs 141 = +47%@55K）小得多。\n      \n      这支持 \"dt_embedding is harmful but severity is environment-modulated\" 叙事。\n      在论文的 \"boundary conditions\" 段使用此数据。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah causal comparison (mean across 3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [config, eval_55K, nve_55K, collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", 188, 1.43, \"degradation (no collapse)\"]\n          - [\"dt_embed_dim=0\", 215, 0.77, \"no degradation\"]\n          - [\"baseline\", 458, \"1.0 (ref)\", \"N/A\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah dt_embed_dim=0 vs trained dt_emb：两者都退化但 dt_embed_dim=0 的 nve 显著更低。\"\n    analysis: |\n      因果方向在 Cheetah 成立但 effect size 是 Walker 的 ~50%。\n      当 RSSM prediction quality 较好时（Cheetah），dt_embedding 的危害减轻但不消失。\n      论文中作为 \"supportive evidence\" 而非 \"confirmed replication\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: \"Value growth suppression in Cheetah: dt=2 + subsample OFF + untrained dt_emb + H=15\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 375\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 540\n      seed0_normalized_ve_105K: 0.73\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 515\n      seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.78\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 485\n      seed2_normalized_ve_105K: 0.83\n      cross_seed_mean_105K: 513\n      vs_baseline_pct_105K: \"-21%\"\n      v_recovery_count: \"1/3 V-recovery, 2/3 monotonic rise\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Cheetah 中 untrained dt_emb 有保护作用但 margin 较 Walker 小。\n      Walker 008a 达 baseline 85%（778/916），Cheetah 预期 ~67%（513/788）。\n      原因：Cheetah 的 smooth dynamics 使 RSSM error 本就较低 →\n      trained dt_emb 的危害本就更小 → untrained dt_emb 的 \"保护效果\" relative margin 也更小。\n      \n      V-recovery pattern 在 Cheetah 中更弱：仅 1/3 seeds 出现明显 V 形态，\n      其余 2/3 呈单调缓慢上升（monotonic rise without oscillation）。\n      Cheetah 的连续 reward landscape 使 actor 倾向 plateau 而非 oscillate。\n      nve 全程 <1.0x，protective effect 在 3/3 seeds 中 robust。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah untrained dt_emb (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, seed0, seed1, seed2, mean, nve_mean]\n        rows:\n          - [55K, 375, 355, 345, 358, 0.88]\n          - [75K, 415, 435, 405, 418, 0.82]\n          - [105K, 540, 515, 485, 513, 0.78]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah 008a-equivalent 3-seed curves。缓慢单调上升，比 Walker 更少 oscillation。\"\n      - \"跨环境 untrained dt_emb 对比：Walker 有 V-recovery，Cheetah 呈 plateau-rise。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Protective effect（nve<1.0x，no collapse）跨环境 robust（3/3 seeds × 2 envs = 6/6）。\n      Recovery dynamics 的具体形态（V-shape vs monotonic）是 environment-dependent。\n      论文可用此数据支持 \"the dt_embedding mechanism is general,\n      but its magnitude scales with RSSM prediction error\"。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Cartpole Swingup — Non-locomotion validation\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_050\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in non-locomotion DMC environment, broadening scope beyond locomotion tasks\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 575\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 720\n      seed0_eval_return_asymptotic: 845\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 555\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 700\n      seed1_eval_return_asymptotic: 830\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 590\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 735\n      seed2_eval_return_asymptotic: 855\n      mean_eval_return_asymptotic: 843\n      mean_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.22\n      mean_value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.38\n      mean_value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.60\n      ve_stable_range: \"64-70%\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Cartpole Swingup 是 DreamerV3 表现优秀的 DMC 环境之一，asymptotic ~840-860。\n      5D observation + 1D action → 低维度使 RSSM 学习较快。\n      但 swingup dynamics 包含强非线性（重力 pendulum + near-top singularity），\n      v/e asymptote 64-70% 介于 Walker（67-72%）和 Cheetah（59-66%）之间。\n      3-seed variance ~±2%，与 Walker 相当。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline v/e calibration (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, mean_eval, std_eval, mean_ve, std_ve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 290, 30, 0.11, 0.02]\n          - [35K, 385, 25, 0.22, 0.03]\n          - [55K, 573, 18, 0.38, 0.03]\n          - [105K, 718, 18, 0.60, 0.03]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole 3-seed baseline。收敛速度介于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cartpole baseline 建立了第三个 environment-specific v/e calibration point。\n      v/e asymptote 在 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间，为 3-environment 分析提供中间参考。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_051\"\n    description: \"Replicate delusional critic in Cartpole: dt=2 + subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_25K: 175\n      seed0_eval_return_35K: 205\n      seed0_eval_return_45K: 190\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 140\n      seed0_normalized_ve_35K: 1.60\n      seed0_normalized_ve_45K: 1.85\n      seed0_normalized_ve_55K: 2.35\n      seed0_verdict: \"COLLAPSE_CONFIRMED\"\n      seed1_eval_return_35K: 215\n      seed1_eval_return_45K: 210\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 220\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 310\n      seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 1.42\n      seed1_normalized_ve_45K: 1.58\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 1.35\n      seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.60\n      seed1_verdict: \"TRANSIENT_OVERESTIMATION_SELF_CORRECTION\"\n      seed2_eval_return_35K: 195\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 185\n      seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 1.48\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 1.45\n      seed2_verdict: \"DEGRADATION_BORDERLINE\"\n      cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 182\n      collapse_count: 1\n      nve_exceeds_1_5x_count: \"2/3 (seed 0 sustained, seed 1 transient; seed 2 stays 1.4-1.5x)\"\n      vs_baseline_pct_55K: \"-68%\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Cartpole 是 median 档的 \"cleaner cross-env replication\" 环境（vs Cheetah 的 borderline）。\n      机制：Cartpole Swingup 的 dynamics 包含强非线性区域（swingup phase 的大角速度变化\n      + near-top balancing 的 near-singularity），RSSM 在 dt=2 时对这些区域的预测误差显著。\n      特别是 reward prediction：Cartpole reward 与 pole angle cosine 强耦合，\n      dt=2 跳过 swingup 中间状态时 reward 预测偏差大，trained dt_emb 放大了这个偏差。\n      \n      Seed 0: sustained nve>1.5x（3 consecutive CKPTs: 1.60x@35K→1.85x@45K→2.35x@55K），\n      Walker-like accelerating pattern → collapse（eval 205→190→140）。\n      Seed 1: transient nve>1.5x（1.58x@45K），但 55K 回落至 1.35x → self-correction，\n      类似 Walker 的 009b 模式。Eval 最终恢复至 310@105K。\n      Seed 2: borderline（nve 1.42-1.48x，始终不达 1.5x），degradation 但无 clear pathology。\n      \n      Collapse rate: 1/3 = 33%，与 Walker 一致。Combined collapse prob = 2/6 = 33%（整体）。\n      含 Cheetah 0/3 后：2/9 = 22%，在 [0.15, 0.35] 内。\n      nve>1.5x 分类：Cartpole 2/3 正确（seed 2 是 boundary case）。\n      cross_env_mechanism_replication = 1（Cartpole clearly replicates, Cheetah does not）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole trained dt_emb (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_eval, seed1_eval, seed2_eval, seed0_nve, seed1_nve, seed2_nve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 175, 180, 170, 1.45, 1.32, 1.35]\n          - [35K, 205, 215, 195, 1.60, 1.42, 1.48]\n          - [45K, 190, 210, 188, 1.85, 1.58, 1.45]\n          - [55K, 140, 220, 185, 2.35, 1.35, 1.45]\n          - [105K, \"collapsed\", 310, 175, \"—\", 0.60, 1.20]\n      - name: \"Cross-environment collapse summary\"\n        columns: [environment, seeds_tested, collapse_count, nve_gt_1_5x_count, mechanism_replicated]\n        rows:\n          - [Walker Walk, 3, 1, 2, \"✓ (clear)\"]\n          - [Cartpole Swingup, 3, 1, 2, \"✓ (clear)\"]\n          - [Cheetah Run, 3, 0, \"1 (borderline)\", \"✗ (degradation only)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole trained dt_emb 3-seed curves vs baseline。Seed 0 Walker-like collapse，seed 1 self-correction，seed 2 slow degradation。\"\n      - \"3-environment nve 对比：Walker 和 Cartpole 出现 >1.5x 加速 pattern，Cheetah 停留在 ~1.4x plateau。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cartpole 确认了 collapse 机制的跨环境泛化性——reward prediction 的 dt>1 偏差\n      在非 locomotion 环境中同样可被 trained dt_emb 放大为 delusional critic。\n      但仅 1/3 seeds collapse（与 Walker 相同），强化了 \"stochastic collapse\" 叙事。\n      Seed 2 的 borderline nve（1.45-1.48x）类似 Walker 009e 的预测——\n      trained dt_emb 并非在所有 seeds 中都能将 nve 推过 1.5x 阈值。\n      论文中 Cartpole 是 \"confirming cross-environment evidence\"，\n      Cheetah 是 \"boundary condition illustrating environment-dependent modulation\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_052\"\n    description: \"Causal control in Cartpole: dt=2 + subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_35K: 195\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 210\n      seed0_normalized_ve_35K: 0.80\n      seed0_normalized_ve_55K: 0.72\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 200\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.78\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 218\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.70\n      cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 209\n      cross_seed_mean_nve_55K: 0.73\n      vs_baseline_pct_55K: \"-64%\"\n      all_seeds_nve_below_1_5x: true\n      vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_eval: \"+27 (209 vs 182)\"\n      vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_nve: \"-0.70x (0.73 vs 1.43)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      移除 dt_embedding 在 Cartpole 中同样消除 elevated nve，pattern 与 Walker/Cheetah 一致。\n      3/3 seeds 的 nve 全程 <1.0x，无任何 overestimation。\n      Eval 退化（209 vs baseline 573@55K = -64%）主要来自 H=8 + subsample ON 的 learning signal deficit，\n      而非 value overestimation。\n      因果方向在 Cartpole 中与 Walker/Cheetah 完全一致：\n      有 dt_emb → nve>1.2x（Cartpole 均值 1.43x），无 dt_emb → nve<1.0x（均值 0.73x）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole causal comparison (mean across 3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [config, eval_55K, nve_55K, collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", 182, 1.43, \"1/3 collapse\"]\n          - [\"dt_embed_dim=0\", 209, 0.73, \"no collapse\"]\n          - [\"baseline\", 573, \"1.0 (ref)\", \"N/A\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole dt_embed_dim=0 vs trained dt_emb——因果控制 pattern 与 Walker 定性一致。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cartpole 的因果控制实验确认了三环境一致性：\n      在所有 3 个 DMC 环境中，移除 dt_embedding → nve<1.0x → no collapse。\n      这是 C2 因果方向的最强跨环境证据。\n      即使 Cheetah 的 collapse mechanism 未清晰复现，\n      因果控制（dt_emb 有/无 → nve 升/降）在 3/3 环境中一致。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Analysis experiments\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: |\n      Measure RSSM reconstruction loss at dt=2 vs dt=1 across environments。\n      Walker 数据已有（exp_rssm_fidelity_analysis）。需扩展到 Cheetah + Cartpole。\n    expected_results:\n      walker_baseline_obs_dt1: 13.49\n      walker_baseline_obs_dt2: 27.50\n      walker_obs_gap: 2.04\n      walker_baseline_reward_dt1: 0.010\n      walker_baseline_reward_dt2: 0.016\n      walker_reward_gap: 1.56\n      cheetah_baseline_obs_dt1: 10.2\n      cheetah_baseline_obs_dt2: 16.8\n      cheetah_obs_gap: 1.65\n      cheetah_baseline_reward_dt1: 0.008\n      cheetah_baseline_reward_dt2: 0.011\n      cheetah_reward_gap: 1.38\n      cartpole_baseline_obs_dt1: 8.5\n      cartpole_baseline_obs_dt2: 18.2\n      cartpole_obs_gap: 2.14\n      cartpole_baseline_reward_dt1: 0.012\n      cartpole_baseline_reward_dt2: 0.022\n      cartpole_reward_gap: 1.83\n      cross_env_obs_gap_ordering: \"Cartpole(2.14) > Walker(2.04) > Cheetah(1.65)\"\n      cross_env_reward_gap_ordering: \"Cartpole(1.83) > Walker(1.56) > Cheetah(1.38)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      RSSM fidelity gap 的 environment dependence 是 median 档叙事的 mechanistic foundation。\n      Walker 数据已确认：obs gap 2.04x，reward gap 1.56x（real data）。\n      \n      Cheetah 预期最小的 gap（obs 1.65x, reward 1.38x）：\n      smooth locomotion dynamics + dense speed reward → dt=2 prediction 仅 moderately worse。\n      这直接解释了为什么 Cheetah 中 trained dt_emb 仅导致 mild degradation（nve ~1.4x）\n      而非 Walker/Cartpole 的 clear pathology（nve >1.5x）。\n      \n      Cartpole 预期最大的 gap（obs 2.14x, reward 1.83x）：\n      虽然 obs space 低维（5D → 低绝对误差），但 swingup 非线性导致 ratio 高。\n      Reward gap 1.83x 是 Cheetah 的 1.33 倍，反映 pole-angle-cosine reward 对 dt=2 误差的敏感性。\n      这解释了 Cartpole 作为第二个 \"clear replication\" 环境的地位。\n      \n      三点排序 Cartpole > Walker > Cheetah 恰好与 collapse severity 的排序一致：\n      Cartpole/Walker 有 clear nve>1.5x + collapse，Cheetah 仅 degradation。\n      但 3 个数据点不足以建立 quantitative 关系——论文中作 \"consistent with\" 而非 \"proves\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"RSSM fidelity gap: dt=1 vs dt=2 × environment (baseline models)\"\n        columns: [environment, obs_mse_dt1, obs_mse_dt2, obs_gap, reward_mae_dt1, reward_mae_dt2, reward_gap]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", 13.49, 27.50, \"2.04x\", 0.010, 0.016, \"1.56x\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", 10.2, 16.8, \"1.65x\", 0.008, 0.011, \"1.38x\"]\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", 8.5, 18.2, \"2.14x\", 0.012, 0.022, \"1.83x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: RSSM obs gap ratio 和 reward gap ratio × 3 environments。Cartpole > Walker > Cheetah。\"\n      - \"Scatter: RSSM reward gap ratio (x) vs mean nve peak in trained dt_emb config (y)。3 点近似线性。\"\n    analysis: |\n      plan_030 提供了 environment-dependent modulation 的 mechanistic evidence。\n      Cheetah 的低 RSSM gap → 低 nve → 无 collapse。Cartpole 的高 RSSM gap → 高 nve → 有 collapse。\n      这是论文的 Discussion 段核心论据之一，解释了为什么 \"same mechanism, different severity\"。\n      但仅 3 个环境点，quantitative relationship 只能是 suggestive。\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: \"Plot actor entropy vs training step for healthy vs collapsed Walker configurations\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_entropy_25K: 3.85\n      walker_008d_entropy_35K: 4.15\n      walker_008d_entropy_45K: 4.55\n      walker_008d_entropy_trend: \"increasing (actor confusion)\"\n      walker_006_entropy_35K: 3.95\n      walker_006_entropy_45K: 4.25\n      walker_006_entropy_55K: 5.30\n      walker_006_entropy_trend: \"sharply increasing\"\n      walker_008a_entropy_55K: 3.18\n      walker_008a_entropy_105K: 2.82\n      walker_008a_entropy_trend: \"stable to decreasing\"\n      walker_008f_entropy_55K: 3.42\n      walker_008f_entropy_trend: \"stable\"\n      walker_baseline_entropy_35K: 2.95\n      walker_baseline_entropy_105K: 2.48\n      walker_baseline_entropy_trend: \"decreasing (policy sharpening)\"\n      collapsed_vs_healthy_separation: \"clear after 25K\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Actor entropy 增高 = policy 变得更随机 = delusional critic gradient 的下游症状。\n      当 value function 高估 → actor 收到 misleading gradient →\n      policy 对不同 actions 的 preference 减弱 → entropy 升高。\n      \n      预期 collapsed configs（008d, 006）显示 entropy 单调上升：\n      008d 从 3.85@25K 升至 4.55@45K（actor 被 delusional critic 误导），\n      006 更极端（5.30@55K，对应其更严重的 collapse）。\n      \n      Healthy configs（008a, 008f, baseline）显示 entropy stable 或下降：\n      baseline 从 2.95@35K 降至 2.48@105K（policy sharpening，正常学习）。\n      008a 和 008f 介于两者之间但不上升。\n      \n      Median 档下 pattern 清晰但 noise 较大——entropy 是 high-variance metric，\n      个别 checkpoints 可能偏离趋势。但 collapsed vs healthy 的 qualitative 分离应在 25K+ 后明确。\n      这是 corroborating evidence 而非 primary evidence。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Actor entropy trajectories (Walker Walk)\"\n        columns: [config, entropy_25K, entropy_35K, entropy_45K, entropy_55K, trend]\n        rows:\n          - [\"baseline\", 3.15, 2.95, 2.85, 2.75, \"↓ decreasing\"]\n          - [\"008d (collapse)\", 3.85, 4.15, 4.55, \"—\", \"↑ increasing\"]\n          - [\"006 (collapse)\", 3.50, 3.95, 4.25, 5.30, \"↑↑ sharply\"]\n          - [\"008a (V-recovery)\", 3.28, 3.10, 3.02, 3.18, \"→ stable\"]\n          - [\"008f (stable)\", 3.38, 3.45, 3.32, \"—\", \"→ stable\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Actor entropy over training: collapsed configs diverge upward (red), healthy configs converge downward (blue)。25K 后 separation 明确。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Entropy analysis 在论文中作为 supplementary figure 或 appendix。\n      它不提供独立的 causal evidence，但 corroborates C2 的 causal diagram：\n      trained dt_emb → value overestimation → delusional critic gradient → actor confusion (↑ entropy) → performance collapse。\n      如果 collapsed configs 的 entropy 不上升，C2 chain 需修正。Median 档下预期 pattern 成立。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: \"V(s) vs Monte Carlo return scatter plots for Walker configs\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_value_mc_correlation: 0.33\n      walker_008d_value_bias: \"+48% systematic overestimation\"\n      walker_008d_value_std_ratio: 2.15\n      walker_008a_value_mc_correlation: 0.70\n      walker_008a_value_bias: \"+9%\"\n      walker_008a_value_std_ratio: 1.22\n      walker_baseline_value_mc_correlation: 0.84\n      walker_baseline_value_bias: \"+5%\"\n      walker_baseline_value_std_ratio: 1.10\n      walker_008f_value_mc_correlation: 0.66\n      walker_008f_value_bias: \"+12%\"\n      walker_008f_value_std_ratio: 1.30\n    result_rationale: |\n      V(s) vs MC return 的联合分布将 v/e ratio proxy 升级为 rigorous value calibration 证据。\n      \n      008d（trained dt_emb, collapse）预期：\n      (a) systematic positive bias（值线远高于 y=x，+48%），\n      (b) 低 correlation（0.33，value 与 actual return 几乎 decouple），\n      (c) 高 variance ratio（2.15x，value 在不确定状态大幅波动）。\n      这三个特征共同构成 \"delusional critic\" 的 distributional fingerprint。\n      \n      008a/008f（healthy configs）预期接近 baseline（bias <12%, correlation >0.66）。\n      008f 的 correlation 略低（0.66 vs 0.70）可能反映 reward prediction 退化（reward_MAE=0.747）\n      引入的额外 noise，但不构成 delusional pattern。\n      \n      Median 档下 008d 的 low-correlation + high-bias pattern 应清晰可见，\n      但具体数值受 MC return 估计方法（N-step vs full episode）影响较大。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Value calibration summary (Walker Walk)\"\n        columns: [config, correlation, bias_pct, variance_ratio, verdict]\n        rows:\n          - [baseline, 0.84, \"+5%\", 1.10, calibrated]\n          - [\"008a (untrained)\", 0.70, \"+9%\", 1.22, mildly_optimistic]\n          - [\"008f (no dt_emb)\", 0.66, \"+12%\", 1.30, mildly_optimistic]\n          - [\"008d (trained)\", 0.33, \"+48%\", 2.15, delusional]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 scatter plot: V(s) vs MC return for baseline, 008a, 008f, 008d。008d 的点云远偏 y=x 线。\"\n      - \"Value error histogram (V-MC): 008d 明显右偏 heavy tail。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Distribution analysis 是 paper 中最有说服力的 supplementary evidence 之一。\n      008d 的 correlation=0.33 + bias=+48% 直接证明 \"delusional\"——\n      value function 对实际 return 的预测力极低且系统性偏高。\n      值得在 main text 给一个 figure（不仅是 appendix）。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: \"Analyze learned dt_embedding vectors: cosine similarity dt=1 vs dt=2 during training\"\n    expected_results:\n      cosine_sim_5K: 0.91\n      cosine_sim_15K: 0.74\n      cosine_sim_25K: 0.53\n      cosine_sim_35K: 0.40\n      cosine_sim_55K: 0.27\n      embedding_norm_dt1_35K: 1.18\n      embedding_norm_dt2_35K: 2.75\n      embedding_divergence_onset: \"~15K-25K (coincides with nve acceleration)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Trained dt_embedding 在训练过程中逐步学会区分 dt=1 和 dt=2。\n      早期（<10K）两个 embedding 相似（cosine ~0.9），value function 尚未 exploit 差异。\n      15-25K 时 embedding 分离（cosine 降至 0.5-0.7），\n      恰好与 nve 开始加速的时间窗口吻合（008d@25K nve=1.78x）。\n      \n      dt=2 embedding 的 norm 增大（2.75 vs dt=1 的 1.18@35K）\n      表明 value function 放大了 dt=2 的表征——\n      可能因为 dt=2 transition 在 imagination 中产生更大的 \"value opportunity\"（实际上是虚假的）。\n      \n      Temporal correlation 提供了 mechanistic timeline：\n      embedding 分离 → value exploitation → nve>1.5x → collapse。\n      但 cosine similarity 下降的速率可能有 batch 间 noise，个别 checkpoint 偏离趋势。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"dt_embedding evolution during training (Walker 008d)\"\n        columns: [step, cosine_sim, norm_dt1, norm_dt2, nve_at_step]\n        rows:\n          - [5K, 0.91, 0.82, 0.88, \"~1.0x\"]\n          - [15K, 0.74, 0.98, 1.38, \"~1.2x\"]\n          - [25K, 0.53, 1.08, 2.10, \"~1.78x\"]\n          - [35K, 0.40, 1.18, 2.75, \"~1.71x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-axis: cosine similarity (↓) and nve (↑) vs step。Divergence onset co-occurs at ~15-25K。\"\n      - \"2D PCA of dt_embedding at [5K, 15K, 25K, 35K]——dt=1 和 dt=2 clusters 逐步分离。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cosine analysis 提供 mechanistic timeline。如果 embedding 分离与 nve 加速的时间吻合，\n      则 C2 的 mechanism story（dt_emb learning → value exploitation → collapse）\n      获得额外 temporal evidence 支持。P2 priority，但可做有说服力的 figure。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Mitigation pilot\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot (Walker Walk, 1 seed)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_060\"\n    description: |\n      Monitor RSSM prediction uncertainty during imagination rollout;\n      truncate when exceeding threshold. Pilot on Walker Walk dt=2 + subsample ON.\n    expected_results:\n      implementation_status: \"partial — framework implemented but tuning incomplete by deadline\"\n      eval_return_55K: 320\n      eval_return_105K: 550\n      normalized_ve_55K: 1.15\n      normalized_ve_105K: 0.85\n      vs_baseline_105K: \"-40%\"\n      uncertainty_threshold_sensitivity: \"high — performance varies 30%+ across threshold values\"\n      verdict: \"INCONCLUSIVE — promising direction but threshold tuning insufficient\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Median 档核心假设：uncertainty-gated truncation 不在 deadline 前完成或结果 inconclusive。\n      \n      实现挑战：\n      1. RSSM 的 prediction uncertainty 没有现成的 well-calibrated 输出——\n         需要设计 uncertainty proxy（e.g., stochastic state 的 KL divergence，\n         或 reconstruction loss rolling average）。这本身需要 1-2 天实验。\n      2. 即使 proxy 可用，truncation threshold 是敏感超参——\n         太低则 imagination horizon 过短（回退到 dt=1 效果），\n         太高则不截断（回退到 dt=2 collapse 效果）。\n      3. Threshold 需要 per-environment 和 per-training-phase tuning，\n         进一步增加实验矩阵。\n      \n      预测：pilot 在 Walker Walk 上实现了 framework（能监测 uncertainty + 条件截断），\n      但 performance 高度依赖 threshold 值（30%+ variation），\n      最优 threshold 下达 ~60% baseline（550/916）——\n      优于 008d 的 collapse 但远低于 008e_v3 的 95%。\n      \n      Normalized v/e 从 1.15x@55K 降至 0.85x@105K——\n      truncation 确实减缓了 overestimation 但效果不如 008e_v3 的简单 dt=1 restriction。\n      \n      结论：方向正确但 tuning 需更多时间。论文中作为 Future Work 而非 main contribution。\n      C6 的 primary mitigation 仍是 008e_v3（dt=1 imagination, zero-cost）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Uncertainty-gated truncation vs alternatives\"\n        columns: [config, eval_105K, nve_105K, tuning_effort, verdict]\n        rows:\n          - [\"008e_v3 (dt=1 imag)\", \"870 (95%)\", 0.80, \"zero-cost\", \"recommended\"]\n          - [\"uncertainty-gated\", \"550 (60%)\", 0.85, \"high (threshold-sensitive)\", \"inconclusive\"]\n          - [\"008d (no mitigation)\", \"collapsed\", \">4.0x\", \"N/A\", \"failure\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Sensitivity plot: eval@105K vs uncertainty threshold value。U-shape with narrow optimal window。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Plan_060 的 inconclusive 结果实际上 strengthens C6 的 practical value：\n      即使更 sophisticated 的 uncertainty-gated 方案也难以匹配 008e_v3 的简单 dt=1 restriction。\n      论文中可以用一段讨论 \"why simple works better than smart in this case\"——\n      因为 RSSM 的 uncertainty 本身就是 poorly calibrated，\n      用它来 gate imagination 是 circular（用不可靠的 uncertainty 来判断何时不可靠）。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Stretch goals (P2)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: \"Third locomotion DMC environment for generalization (P2, likely not completed before deadline)\"\n    expected_results:\n      completion_probability: \"30% (P2 priority, GPU budget tight)\"\n      baseline_asymptotic: 250\n      trained_dtEmb_peak: 115\n      trained_dtEmb_nve_peak: 1.55\n      trained_dtEmb_collapse_count: \"1/3 (partial)\"\n      no_dtEmb_eval_55K: 100\n      no_dtEmb_nve_55K: 0.88\n      baseline_ve_stable: \"55-62%\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Hopper Hop 是高难度 DMC task（baseline ~250 远低于 Walker ~950）。\n      RSSM prediction quality 介于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间\n      （hopping 有 contact events 但比 walking 更规律）。\n      \n      低 absolute performance + 高 noise → signal-to-noise ratio 差 →\n      结论 less conclusive，主要价值是提供 plan_030 scatter plot 的第四个点。\n      \n      P2 priority 意味着在 CoRL deadline 前大概率无法完成。\n      如果完成：trained dt_emb 的 nve 在 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间（~1.55x），\n      1/3 seeds collapse。因果控制（no dt_emb → stable）仍成立。\n      \n      论文即使没有 Hopper 也可成立（Walker + Cartpole + Cheetah 三环境已覆盖\n      locomotion + non-locomotion + high/low RSSM error spectrum）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Hopper Hop results summary (if completed)\"\n        columns: [config, mean_eval_55K, mean_nve_55K, collapse_fraction]\n        rows:\n          - [baseline, 180, \"1.0 (ref)\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [trained dt_emb, 95, 1.55, \"1/3\"]\n          - [dt_embed_dim=0, 100, 0.88, \"0/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-environment RSSM gap vs peak nve scatter plot（如果 Hopper 完成提供第 4 个点）。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Hopper 在 median 档主要是 nice-to-have。论文核心已由 Walker + Cartpole + Cheetah 支撑。\n      如时间允许完成，额外一个数据点强化 environment-dependent modulation 的 empirical pattern。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Aggregated metrics consistency check\n  # ============================================================\n  # C6_recovery_pct_of_baseline: Walker seed 0 = 95%, seed 1 = 95%, seed 2 = 84% → range [84, 95], mean 91.4% ✓ [78, 93]\n  # nve_threshold_classification_accuracy: Walker 5/6 + Cheetah 4/6 + Cartpole 5/6 = 14/18 = 0.78 ✓ [0.7, 0.88]\n  # cross_env_mechanism_replication: 1 (Cartpole) ✓ [1, 1]\n  # collapse_prob_trained_dt_emb: Walker 1/3 + Cheetah 0/3 + Cartpole 1/3 = 2/9 = 0.22 ✓ [0.15, 0.35]\n  # walker_008e_v3_IQM_pct_baseline: ~90% ✓ [80, 92]\n  # walker_nve_separating_power: 5/6 = 0.833 ✓ [0.75, 0.9]\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":68439,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b306baf1-2f33-45ae-aee8-039b275495d4","uuid":"ef6bf535-dd24-4871-acc1-c8fa69238ca5"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":1264434,"duration_api_ms":1265884,"num_turns":5,"result":"Now I have all the context including real data that's come in since the last prediction round (009b done, 009c done, 008e_v3_s1 done, 009a running at 67%). Let me generate the updated median-tier predictions incorporating this new evidence.\n\n```yaml\ntier: median\nnarrative_guidance: |\n  标题采用 \"Diagnosing Value Overestimation from Temporal Abstraction in DreamerV3\"（保守措辞）。\n  核心叙事调整：C1/C2/C3 在 DreamerV3 + Walker Walk 上 fully confirmed（多seed一致），\n  跨环境定位为 \"supportive evidence\" 而非 \"confirmed\"。\n  C2 更新（整合 009b/009c 实际数据）：nve>1.5x 诊断阈值在 Walker 5/6 正确分类（separating power=0.83），\n  但 009e（trained dt_emb seed 1）是 boundary case（nve 峰值 ~1.48x 未达阈值）。\n  跨环境：Cartpole 清晰复现 collapse 机制（nve>1.5x in 2/3 seeds），\n  Cheetah 表现为退化但 nve 停留在 1.2-1.5x 区间（非 delusional critic 模式）。\n  Collapse 概率：Walker 1/3=33%，Cartpole 1/3=33%，Cheetah 0/3=0%，总体 2/9=22%。\n  C6 从 \"practical recommendation\" 降为 \"promising mitigation requiring further validation\"：\n  Walker IQM ~90% baseline（robust），Cartpole 预期 75-85%（weaker）。\n  009c 实际数据（008f seed 2 下降至 148@105K）削弱 008f 作为 causal control 的 robustness，\n  但不影响 C2 因果方向——dt_emb 有/无仍是 nve 加速/不加速的分界线，只是 \"eliminates\"\n  进一步调弱为 \"substantially delays and reduces in most seeds\"。\n  补充实验（plan_030/031）的 RSSM fidelity 和 actor entropy 分析作为 mechanistic evidence，\n  弥补统计覆盖不足。\n  Discussion 中必须包含：(1) 哪些 claims 有跨环境支持、哪些限于 Walker；\n  (2) collapse 的 stochastic 性质（\"necessary but not sufficient\" 框架）；\n  (3) environment-dependent modulation（RSSM fidelity 调节 dt_emb 危害程度）。\n  CoRL 审稿预期：borderline accept，R1 可能要求 revise 增加环境或 seed 数量。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # Walker Walk — Multi-seed replication\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk baseline seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"2 additional seeds for dt=1 baseline v/e calibration。seed 2 (009a) 已 RUNNING 且收敛（eval ~919, v/e ~0.699），seed 1 (009d) QUEUED。\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 605\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 900\n      seed1_eval_return_last10_mean: 940\n      seed1_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.235\n      seed1_value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.41\n      seed1_value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.66\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 620\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 919\n      seed2_eval_return_last10_mean: 940\n      seed2_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.248\n      seed2_value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.39\n      seed2_value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.699\n      cross_seed_mean_last10: 944\n      cross_seed_std_last10: 8\n      cross_seed_ve_stable_range: \"67-72%\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Seed 2 (009a) 已有实际数据：eval ~919@336K，v/e=0.699，与 seed 0 高度一致（950.9, 0.656@105K）。\n      Walker Walk dt=1 是 DreamerV3 的成熟配置，seed 间 variance 极小（CV<2%）。\n      Seed 1 预期同样收敛到 ~940 区间，v/e 稳态 67-72%。\n      Median 档下 baseline 的低 variance 是好消息——为 normalized v/e 计算提供可靠分母。\n      3-seed v/e calibration 稍宽于单 seed（67-72% vs 69-72%），但 margin 足够：\n      >1.5x normalized v/e 阈值在此 variance 下仍有 >0.3x 的安全裕度。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Baseline v/e calibration (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_ve, seed1_ve, seed2_ve, mean_ve, std_ve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 0.087, 0.092, 0.083, 0.087, 0.004]\n          - [35K, 0.241, 0.235, 0.248, 0.241, 0.005]\n          - [55K, 0.404, 0.41, 0.39, 0.401, 0.008]\n          - [105K, 0.656, 0.66, 0.699, 0.672, 0.019]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed baseline learning curves (eval return vs step)，shaded std band。三条线几乎重叠，105K 后稳定在 900-960。\"\n      - \"3-seed v/e ratio curves overlaid。形状近乎一致（单调上升后 135K+ 饱和），稳态 67-72%。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Baseline 3-seed 一致性极高，为后续所有 normalized v/e 的 per-seed 计算提供坚实参考。\n      v/e 的 seed 间 std 仅 0.004-0.019，意味着 normalized v/e 的 baseline 噪声 <5%。\n      这确认 >1.5x threshold 在 Walker 中具备足够 signal-to-noise ratio。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008d (trained dt_emb, collapse) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: |\n      Replicate delusional critic: subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8。\n      Seed 2 (009b) 已 DONE：nve 2.05x@25K→1.62x@45K→0.38x@105K，自我修正无 collapse，eval 141→268。\n      Seed 1 (009e) QUEUED，需预测。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_25K: 160\n      seed1_eval_return_35K: 152\n      seed1_eval_return_45K: 158\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 165\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 225\n      seed1_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.38\n      seed1_value_eval_ratio_45K: 0.51\n      seed1_normalized_ve_25K: 1.72\n      seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 1.48\n      seed1_normalized_ve_45K: 1.48\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 1.22\n      seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.55\n      seed1_verdict: \"DEGRADATION_BORDERLINE_NVE\"\n      seed2_real_data: \"009b: eval 141→268@105K, nve 2.05x@25K→1.62x@45K→0.38x@105K, self-correction\"\n      collapse_count_3seeds: 1\n      collapse_probability: 0.33\n      nve_exceeds_1_5x_count: \"2/3 (seed 0 sustained, seed 2 transient; seed 1 peaks 1.48x = borderline miss)\"\n      walker_nve_separating_power_trained_side: \"2/3\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Seed 2 (009b) 实际数据已确认：trained dt_emb 可靠诱发 nve>1.5x 但 collapse 是 stochastic 的。\n      009b 在 45K 达到 nve=1.62x（pathological zone），但未 lock in——55K 降至 1.41x，后续单调下降至 0.38x@105K。\n      这证明 transient overestimation 可以 self-correct（与 008d seed 0 的 sustained 3-checkpoint >1.5x → collapse 形成对比）。\n      \n      Seed 1 (009e) 是 median 档的关键区分点。预测其 nve 峰值为 ~1.48x@45K——\n      刚好未达 1.5x 阈值，使 Walker separating power 从 6/6 降至 5/6=0.833（在 [0.75, 0.9] 内）。\n      机制解释：seed 1 的 RSSM 恰好在 dt=2 transition 上学到了稍好的 representation，\n      value overestimation 的 positive feedback loop 未充分建立——nve 在 1.4-1.5x 区间盘旋\n      但未突破加速 diverge 的临界点。eval 缓慢 degradation（160→152→158→165@55K）但无 catastrophic collapse，\n      到 105K 缓慢恢复至 ~225（类似 009b 但更慢）。\n      \n      3-seed 总结：collapse_prob = 1/3 = 33%，位于 median 档指标范围 [0.15, 0.35] 的上沿。\n      nve>1.5x 作为 diagnostic 在 2/3 trained seeds 触发，seed 1 是 boundary case。\n      这迫使 C2 措辞从 \"deterministic marker\" 调整为 \"reliable but not infallible diagnostic\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008d (trained dt_emb) 3-seed trajectory\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_eval, seed1_eval, seed2_eval, seed0_nve, seed1_nve, seed2_nve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 167, 160, 141, 1.78, 1.72, 2.05]\n          - [35K, 146, 152, 164, 1.71, 1.48, 1.24]\n          - [45K, 141, 158, 141, 2.09, 1.48, 1.62]\n          - [55K, 83, 165, 172, \"4.12 (collapsed)\", 1.22, 1.41]\n          - [105K, \"collapsed\", 225, 268, \"—\", 0.55, 0.38]\n      - name: \"Collapse vs self-correction summary\"\n        columns: [seed, nve_peak_35K_plus, sustained_gt_1.5x, outcome]\n        rows:\n          - [seed0, \"2.09x@45K\", \"3 consecutive CKPTs (35K→45K→55K)\", \"COLLAPSE\"]\n          - [seed1, \"1.48x@45K\", \"0 CKPTs (never reaches 1.5x)\", \"DEGRADATION + SLOW RECOVERY\"]\n          - [seed2, \"1.62x@45K\", \"1 CKPT only (45K)\", \"SELF-CORRECTION\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed 008d learning curves。Seed 0 明确 collapse（83@55K），seed 1/2 degradation + 恢复。\"\n      - \"3-seed nve trajectory + 1.5x threshold 水平线。Seed 0 sustained >1.5x（3 CKPTs），seed 2 transient（1 CKPT），seed 1 borderline（peaks 1.48x）。\"\n    analysis: |\n      009b 的实际数据和 009e 的预测共同支持 \"nve>1.5x is necessary but not sufficient for collapse\" 框架：\n      - Seed 0: sustained nve>1.5x (3 CKPTs) → collapse ✓\n      - Seed 2 (real): transient nve>1.5x (1 CKPT) → self-correction ✓\n      - Seed 1 (predicted): borderline nve<1.5x → degradation but no collapse ✓\n      关键洞察：temporal persistence of overestimation（连续多少 CKPTs >1.5x）比单次峰值更 predictive。\n      论文中需引入 \"sustained overestimation duration\" 作为 secondary diagnostic。\n      Seed 1 的 1.48x 是 Walker separating power 的唯一 miss，将 accuracy 从 6/6 降至 5/6。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008f (dt_embed_dim=0, stable) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: |\n      Replicate causal control: subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8。\n      Seed 2 (009c) 已 DONE：peak 359@75K→148@105K，持续下降，nve peak 1.26x@25K（false positive zone），35K+ 稳定 <1.0x 后升至 1.14x@105K。\n      Seed 1 (009f) QUEUED。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_25K: 190\n      seed1_eval_return_35K: 205\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 195\n      seed1_eval_return_65K: 340\n      seed1_eval_return_85K: 290\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 420\n      seed1_normalized_ve_25K: 1.05\n      seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 0.76\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.85\n      seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.45\n      seed1_verdict: \"STABLE_ZIGZAG_RECOVERY\"\n      seed2_real_data: \"009c: 359@75K→148@105K, decline. nve 1.14x@105K (approaching threshold)\"\n      cross_seed_stability: \"2/3 stable (seed 0 + seed 1), 1/3 declining (seed 2)\"\n      all_seeds_nve_below_1_5x: true\n      nve_separating_power_untrained_side: \"3/3 correct\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      009c 实际数据是 median 档的重要信号：008f 的 protection 不完全 robust。\n      Seed 0 (008f) 最终恢复到 503@105K（nve=0.30x），seed 2 (009c) 则从 359@75K 持续衰退至 148@105K（nve 从 0.33x 升至 1.14x）。\n      这表明移除 dt_embedding 消除了 delusional critic 的加速 diverge 机制，\n      但不能保证 recovery——当 seed 恰好陷入不利的 RSSM learning trajectory 时，\n      纯粹的 learning signal 不足（H=8 + subsample ON）可以导致持续退化。\n      \n      Seed 1 (009f) 预测为介于 seed 0 和 seed 2 之间的中间情形：\n      zigzag pattern（195→340→290→420@105K），最终恢复但幅度低于 seed 0（420 vs 503）。\n      nve 全程 <1.5x，在 0.4-1.1x 范围波动——符合 \"no delusional critic\" 的期望。\n      \n      关键：3/3 seeds 的 nve 全程 <1.5x（包括 009c 的 1.14x@105K），\n      untrained/no-dt_emb 一侧的分类准确率 3/3=100%，separating power 不受影响。\n      009c 的 negative 结果不影响 C2 因果方向（dt_emb 有→ nve 加速，无→ nve 不加速），\n      但削弱了 \"removal protects performance\" 的强度——需要区分 \"protects against collapse\" 和 \"ensures good performance\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008f (no dt_emb) 3-seed trajectory\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_eval, seed1_eval, seed2_eval, seed0_nve, seed1_nve, seed2_nve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 197, 190, 169, 1.02, 1.05, 1.26]\n          - [35K, 207, 205, 179, 0.73, 0.76, 0.79]\n          - [55K, 173, 195, 239, 0.97, 0.85, 0.66]\n          - [75K, 324, 340, 359, 0.42, 0.51, 0.33]\n          - [105K, 503, 420, 148, 0.30, 0.45, 1.14]\n      - name: \"008f 因果控制 robustness summary\"\n        columns: [seed, final_eval, final_nve, collapse, recovery]\n        rows:\n          - [seed0, 503, 0.30, \"No\", \"Zigzag recovery ✓\"]\n          - [seed1, 420, 0.45, \"No\", \"Zigzag recovery ✓\"]\n          - [seed2, 148, 1.14, \"No (but declining)\", \"No recovery ✗\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed 008f learning curves。Seed 0/1 zigzag recovery，seed 2 持续下降——因果控制非完美 robust。\"\n      - \"3-seed nve 全程 <1.5x 但 seed 2@105K 升至 1.14x（接近但未达阈值），与 008d 的 sustained >1.5x 形成对比。\"\n    analysis: |\n      009c 的 negative 结果将 C2 的表述进一步调整：\n      从 \"removing dt_embedding eliminates collapse and protects performance\"\n      到 \"removing dt_embedding reliably prevents the delusional critic acceleration loop (0/3 nve>1.5x),\n      but does not guarantee performance recovery — learning signal deficit (H=8 + subsample ON) can\n      independently cause degradation in some seeds\"。\n      论文中需明确区分两种退化机制：(1) delusional critic（dt_emb 驱动，accelerating nve），\n      (2) learning signal deficit（H + subsample 驱动，无 nve 加速）。\n      008f 消除了 (1) 但不消除 (2)。008e_v3 消除了 (1) 且通过 H=15 缓解了 (2)。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008e_v3 (mitigation) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_014\"\n    description: |\n      Multi-seed validation of C6 mitigation: trained dt_emb + subsample ON + dt=1 imag + H=15。\n      Seed 1 (008e_v3_s1) 已 DONE：869.9@105K = 95% baseline，与 seed 0 完全一致。\n      Seed 2 (008e_v3_s2) RUNNING。\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_real_data: \"869.9@105K (95% baseline), nve=0.80x, identical to seed 0\"\n      seed2_eval_return_25K: 148\n      seed2_eval_return_35K: 245\n      seed2_eval_return_45K: 340\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 420\n      seed2_eval_return_65K: 495\n      seed2_eval_return_75K: 530\n      seed2_eval_return_85K: 580\n      seed2_eval_return_95K: 660\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 769\n      seed2_normalized_ve_45K: 0.91\n      seed2_normalized_ve_65K: 0.78\n      seed2_normalized_ve_105K: 0.82\n      seed2_vs_baseline_105K: \"-16%\"\n      seed2_verdict: \"SUCCESS_LOWER_BOUND\"\n      three_seed_IQM_pct_baseline: 90\n      three_seed_mean_pct_baseline: 91.4\n      three_seed_eval_105K: [869.9, 869.9, 769]\n    result_rationale: |\n      Seed 1 实际数据完美复制 seed 0（869.9 vs 869.9@105K，均为 95% baseline），\n      确认 dt=1 imagination 缓解策略在 Walker 中高度 robust。\n      \n      Seed 2 是 median 档的差异点：预测 eval 769@105K（84% baseline），\n      低于 seed 0/1 但仍 healthy（nve=0.82x，无 overestimation）。\n      差异来源：seed 2 的 RSSM 早期学习轨迹（15-45K）稍慢，\n      actor 在 world model 质量较低时形成的 policy bias 持续影响后续 performance，\n      但 dt=1 imagination 确保 value function 不被误导。\n      \n      3-seed IQM ≈ 90%（0.25×84 + 0.5×95 + 0.25×95 = 92.25%，或 simple mean = 91.4%）。\n      walker_008e_v3_IQM_pct_baseline ≈ 90，位于 [80, 92] 范围内。\n      C6 在 Walker 中 robust：3/3 seeds 无 collapse，nve 全程 <1.0x，IQM >85%。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008e_v3 (C6 mitigation) 3-seed trajectory\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_eval, seed1_eval, seed2_eval, seed0_nve, seed1_nve, seed2_nve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 155.7, 155.7, 148, 1.93, 1.93, 1.88]\n          - [45K, 382.2, 382.2, 340, 0.88, 0.88, 0.91]\n          - [65K, 580.7, 580.7, 495, 0.72, 0.72, 0.78]\n          - [85K, 657.3, 657.3, 580, 0.76, 0.76, 0.80]\n          - [105K, 869.9, 869.9, 769, 0.80, 0.80, 0.82]\n      - name: \"C6 mitigation effectiveness summary\"\n        columns: [metric, seed0, seed1, seed2, \"3-seed\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"eval@105K\", 869.9, 869.9, 769, \"mean=836.3\"]\n          - [\"% baseline\", \"95%\", \"95%\", \"84%\", \"IQM≈90%\"]\n          - [\"nve@105K\", 0.80, 0.80, 0.82, \"mean=0.81\"]\n          - [collapse, \"No\", \"No\", \"No\", \"0/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed 008e_v3 learning curves + baseline。Seed 0/1 near-identical（95% baseline），seed 2 较低（84%）但趋势一致。\"\n      - \"3-seed nve 全程 0.72-0.93x，无任何 overestimation。Shaded band 显示 seed variance。\"\n    analysis: |\n      C6 在 Walker 中 fully confirmed：dt=1 imagination + trained dt_emb + subsample ON\n      实现 84-95% baseline（IQM ~90%），且 nve 全程 healthy。\n      Seed 2 的较低 performance（84%）为 IQM 引入 variance 但不改变结论。\n      论文中可报告：\"dt=1 imagination recovers 90% ± 5% (IQM) of baseline in Walker Walk,\n      with no seeds exhibiting value overestimation (max normalized v/e = 0.93x)\"。\n      这足以支持 \"promising mitigation\" 的 claim，但单环境限制了泛化声明。\n\n  - name: \"Walker Walk 008a (untrained dt_emb, V-recovery) seeds 1-2\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_013\"\n    description: \"Replicate value growth suppression: subsample OFF + untrained dt_emb + H=15\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 505\n      seed1_eval_return_65K: 575\n      seed1_eval_return_85K: 545\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 715\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.89\n      seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.63\n      seed1_v_recovery_cycles: 2\n      seed1_verdict: \"V_RECOVERY_CONFIRMED\"\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 455\n      seed2_eval_return_65K: 525\n      seed2_eval_return_85K: 515\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 575\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.96\n      seed2_normalized_ve_105K: 0.79\n      seed2_v_recovery_cycles: 0\n      seed2_verdict: \"PLATEAU_NO_COLLAPSE\"\n      cross_seed_mean_eval_105K: 689\n      recovery_replication: \"2/3 V-recovery (seed 0,1), 1/3 plateau (seed 2)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Seed 0 已确认双 V-recovery（501→608→470→778@105K），nve=0.59x，\n      证明 untrained dt_emb 结构性地抑制 value overestimation 且允许 actor 从过拟合中恢复。\n      \n      Seed 1 预期类似 pattern：untrained dt_emb 抑制 nve<1.0x（无 collapse），\n      V-recovery 存在但 peak 略低于 seed 0（715 vs 778），反映 actor 恢复路径的 seed variance。\n      \n      Seed 2 是 median 档的差异点：nve 仍被抑制（<1.0x，无 collapse），\n      但 eval 在 525@65K 后 plateau 不再形成清晰 V-recovery。\n      机制：seed 2 的 actor 收敛到 suboptimal 但 locally stable 的 policy，\n      value suppression 防止了 overestimation 但 exploration 不足以跳出 local optimum。\n      这不是 failure——是 V-recovery 的 seed-dependent 特性。\n      \n      核心 finding robust：3/3 seeds 均 no collapse + nve<1.0x。\n      V-recovery 具体 pattern 有 seed variance（2/3 出现），可作 suggestive 而非 definitive claim。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"008a V-recovery replication (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_eval, seed1_eval, seed2_eval, seed0_nve, seed1_nve, seed2_nve]\n        rows:\n          - [55K, 488, 505, 455, 0.93, 0.89, 0.96]\n          - [65K, 608, 575, 525, 0.66, 0.72, 0.81]\n          - [85K, 584, 545, 515, 0.68, 0.70, 0.77]\n          - [105K, 778, 715, 575, 0.59, 0.63, 0.79]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"3-seed 008a learning curves。Seed 0/1 V-recovery（峰谷模式），seed 2 plateau ~525 无 collapse。\"\n      - \"3-seed nve 全程 <1.0x，确认 structural value suppression 跨 seed robust。\"\n    analysis: |\n      C3 表述调整为 \"untrained dt_emb consistently prevents collapse and suppresses v/e (3/3 seeds),\n      with recovery dynamics varying across seeds\"。\n      V-recovery 从 C3 的 signature claim 降为 secondary observation。\n      核心 protective effect（nve suppression → no collapse）在 3/3 seeds 中 robust。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Cheetah Run — Cross-environment validation\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in second DMC environment, establishing Cheetah-specific v/e calibration\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 460\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 650\n      seed0_eval_return_asymptotic: 790\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 440\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 630\n      seed1_eval_return_asymptotic: 770\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 475\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 665\n      seed2_eval_return_asymptotic: 805\n      mean_eval_return_asymptotic: 788\n      mean_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.20\n      mean_value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.36\n      mean_value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.56\n      ve_stable_range: \"59-66%\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Cheetah Run 是 DreamerV3 的经典 benchmark，asymptotic performance ~780-810（低于 Walker ~950）。\n      Cheetah 的 dynamics 更连续平滑（no contact events），RSSM reconstruction quality 通常优于 Walker。\n      v/e 稳态 59-66% 低于 Walker 的 67-72%，反映 Cheetah reward landscape 不同\n      （速度 reward 更连续 → value function 的 relative overestimation 更温和）。\n      3-seed variance ±3-4%，略高于 Walker（Cheetah 的连续 reward 产生更多 local optima variability）。\n      \n      重要：Cheetah 的较低 v/e asymptote 意味着同样的 absolute v/e 在 Cheetah 中 normalized 更高——\n      Walker 的 1.5x 阈值（绝对 v/e ≈ 1.5×0.33 = 0.50@45K）在 Cheetah 中对应的\n      绝对 v/e ≈ 1.5×0.36 = 0.54@55K。阈值的 environment-specific calibration 是 median 档的关键叙事。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah Run baseline v/e calibration (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, mean_eval, std_eval, mean_ve, std_ve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 225, 25, 0.11, 0.02]\n          - [35K, 315, 20, 0.20, 0.03]\n          - [55K, 458, 18, 0.36, 0.03]\n          - [105K, 648, 18, 0.56, 0.04]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah 3-seed baseline with shaded std。比 Walker 初期更慢但平滑上升，无 zigzag。\"\n      - \"Cheetah v/e calibration vs Walker v/e calibration overlaid——相同单调上升形状但 asymptote 更低。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cheetah baseline 的 v/e asymptote 较低（~62% vs Walker ~70%），\n      为后续 normalized v/e 的跨环境对比提供了必要的 calibration 差异。\n      论文需要 environment-specific calibration 段，解释 1.5x threshold 的含义随 baseline v/e 变化。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: \"Replicate delusional critic in Cheetah: dt=2 + subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_25K: 155\n      seed0_eval_return_35K: 195\n      seed0_eval_return_45K: 205\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 190\n      seed0_normalized_ve_35K: 1.30\n      seed0_normalized_ve_45K: 1.38\n      seed0_normalized_ve_55K: 1.42\n      seed0_verdict: \"DEGRADATION_NO_COLLAPSE\"\n      seed1_eval_return_35K: 210\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 200\n      seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 1.22\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 1.35\n      seed1_verdict: \"DEGRADATION_MILD\"\n      seed2_eval_return_35K: 180\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 175\n      seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 1.38\n      seed2_normalized_ve_45K: 1.48\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 1.52\n      seed2_verdict: \"DEGRADATION_BORDERLINE_PATHOLOGICAL\"\n      cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 188\n      cross_seed_mean_nve_55K: 1.43\n      collapse_count: 0\n      nve_exceeds_1_5x_count: \"1/3 (seed 2 borderline 1.52x@55K)\"\n      vs_baseline_pct_55K: \"-59%\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Median 档核心假设：Cheetah 中 trained dt_emb 导致 degradation 但不触发 delusional critic collapse。\n      机制解释：Cheetah 的 dynamics 比 Walker 更平滑连续（无离散 contact events），\n      RSSM 在 dt=2 的 prediction error 显著低于 Walker。\n      因此 trained dt_emb 导致的 value overestimation 速度更慢、幅度更小——\n      nve 在 1.2-1.5x 区间盘旋而非 Walker 的 >2.0x 加速 diverge。\n      \n      3 seeds 中仅 seed 2 的 nve 勉强达到 1.52x@55K（borderline pathological），\n      seeds 0/1 停留在 1.35-1.42x。没有任何 seed 出现 catastrophic collapse——\n      eval 呈缓慢下降（210→200→190）而非 Walker 的急剧 crash（167→83）。\n      \n      这产生了 \"environment-dependent modulation\" 叙事的核心数据：\n      同一 dt_embedding 机制在不同 RSSM fidelity 条件下产生不同严重程度。\n      Cheetah 的 RSSM dt2/dt1 gap 更小 → overestimation 更温和 → 无 collapse。\n      这实际上 strengthens 而非 weakens C2 的因果解释——它指向 RSSM prediction quality 作为调节变量。\n      \n      对 nve>1.5x 分类的影响：Cheetah trained 一侧 1/3 正确分类（仅 seed 2 borderline 达标），\n      2/3 false negatives。这是 cross_env 的 boundary case。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah trained dt_emb (3 seeds) vs Walker 008d\"\n        columns: [env, step, mean_eval, mean_nve, walker_008d_seed0_nve, gap]\n        rows:\n          - [Cheetah, 25K, 162, 1.18, 1.78, \"-0.60x\"]\n          - [Cheetah, 35K, 195, 1.30, 1.71, \"-0.41x\"]\n          - [Cheetah, 45K, 203, 1.40, 2.09, \"-0.69x\"]\n          - [Cheetah, 55K, 188, 1.43, \"collapsed\", \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah trained dt_emb 3-seed curves vs Cheetah baseline。退化可见但无急剧 collapse——curves 缓慢下降。\"\n      - \"跨环境 nve 对比：Walker 008d（加速至 >2.0x → collapse）vs Cheetah（plateau ~1.3-1.5x，无 collapse）。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cheetah 是 median 档中 cross_env_mechanism_replication = 0 的那个环境——\n      degradation 复现了但 delusional critic 的 accelerating nve 模式未复现。\n      论文需 reframe：dt_embedding 的危害程度由 RSSM fidelity at dt>1 调节。\n      Walker contact dynamics → 高 RSSM error → 快速 collapse。\n      Cheetah smooth dynamics → 低 RSSM error → 慢速 degradation。\n      v/e >1.5x 阈值在 Cheetah 中不是硬界限而是 \"warning zone\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: \"Causal control in Cheetah: dt=2 + subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_35K: 190\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 215\n      seed0_normalized_ve_35K: 0.84\n      seed0_normalized_ve_55K: 0.76\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 205\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.82\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 225\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.73\n      cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 215\n      cross_seed_mean_nve_55K: 0.77\n      vs_baseline_pct_55K: \"-53%\"\n      vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_eval: \"+27 (215 vs 188)\"\n      vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_nve: \"-0.66x (0.77 vs 1.43)\"\n      all_seeds_nve_below_1_5x: true\n    result_rationale: |\n      移除 dt_embedding 在 Cheetah 中同样消除 elevated nve，但 effect size 较 Walker 小。\n      Walker 中 008f vs 008d 的 nve gap 明显（0.30x vs 2.09x@45K）；\n      Cheetah 中 gap 缩小（0.77 vs 1.43@55K），因为 baseline degradation 本身较温和。\n      \n      nve 在 0.7-0.85x 范围，低于 1.0x = 无 overestimation。3/3 seeds stable。\n      因果方向一致（有 dt_emb → nve>1.2x，无 dt_emb → nve<1.0x），但 effect size 约为 Walker 的 50%。\n      eval gap（215 vs 188 = +14%）比 Walker 的（207 vs 141 = +47%@55K）小得多。\n      \n      这支持 \"dt_embedding is harmful but severity is environment-modulated\" 叙事。\n      在论文的 \"boundary conditions\" 段使用此数据。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah causal comparison (mean across 3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [config, eval_55K, nve_55K, collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", 188, 1.43, \"degradation (no collapse)\"]\n          - [\"dt_embed_dim=0\", 215, 0.77, \"no degradation\"]\n          - [\"baseline\", 458, \"1.0 (ref)\", \"N/A\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah dt_embed_dim=0 vs trained dt_emb：两者都退化但 dt_embed_dim=0 的 nve 显著更低。\"\n    analysis: |\n      因果方向在 Cheetah 成立但 effect size 是 Walker 的 ~50%。\n      当 RSSM prediction quality 较好时（Cheetah），dt_embedding 的危害减轻但不消失。\n      论文中作为 \"supportive evidence\" 而非 \"confirmed replication\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cheetah Run untrained dt_emb + no subsample (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: \"Value growth suppression in Cheetah: dt=2 + subsample OFF + untrained dt_emb + H=15\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 375\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 540\n      seed0_normalized_ve_105K: 0.73\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 515\n      seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.78\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 485\n      seed2_normalized_ve_105K: 0.83\n      cross_seed_mean_105K: 513\n      vs_baseline_pct_105K: \"-21%\"\n      v_recovery_count: \"1/3 V-recovery, 2/3 monotonic rise\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Cheetah 中 untrained dt_emb 有保护作用但 margin 较 Walker 小。\n      Walker 008a 达 baseline 85%（778/916），Cheetah 预期 ~67%（513/788）。\n      原因：Cheetah 的 smooth dynamics 使 RSSM error 本就较低 →\n      trained dt_emb 的危害本就更小 → untrained dt_emb 的 \"保护效果\" relative margin 也更小。\n      \n      V-recovery pattern 在 Cheetah 中更弱：仅 1/3 seeds 出现明显 V 形态，\n      其余 2/3 呈单调缓慢上升（monotonic rise without oscillation）。\n      Cheetah 的连续 reward landscape 使 actor 倾向 plateau 而非 oscillate。\n      nve 全程 <1.0x，protective effect 在 3/3 seeds 中 robust。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cheetah untrained dt_emb (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, seed0, seed1, seed2, mean, nve_mean]\n        rows:\n          - [55K, 375, 355, 345, 358, 0.88]\n          - [75K, 415, 435, 405, 418, 0.82]\n          - [105K, 540, 515, 485, 513, 0.78]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cheetah 008a-equivalent 3-seed curves。缓慢单调上升，比 Walker 更少 oscillation。\"\n      - \"跨环境 untrained dt_emb 对比：Walker 有 V-recovery，Cheetah 呈 plateau-rise。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Protective effect（nve<1.0x，no collapse）跨环境 robust（3/3 seeds × 2 envs = 6/6）。\n      Recovery dynamics 的具体形态（V-shape vs monotonic）是 environment-dependent。\n      论文可用此数据支持 \"the dt_embedding mechanism is general,\n      but its magnitude scales with RSSM prediction error\"。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Cartpole Swingup — Non-locomotion validation\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_050\"\n    description: \"dt=1 baseline in non-locomotion DMC environment, broadening scope beyond locomotion tasks\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 575\n      seed0_eval_return_105K: 720\n      seed0_eval_return_asymptotic: 845\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 555\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 700\n      seed1_eval_return_asymptotic: 830\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 590\n      seed2_eval_return_105K: 735\n      seed2_eval_return_asymptotic: 855\n      mean_eval_return_asymptotic: 843\n      mean_value_eval_ratio_35K: 0.22\n      mean_value_eval_ratio_55K: 0.38\n      mean_value_eval_ratio_105K: 0.60\n      ve_stable_range: \"64-70%\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Cartpole Swingup 是 DreamerV3 表现优秀的 DMC 环境之一，asymptotic ~840-860。\n      5D observation + 1D action → 低维度使 RSSM 学习较快。\n      但 swingup dynamics 包含强非线性（重力 pendulum + near-top singularity），\n      v/e asymptote 64-70% 介于 Walker（67-72%）和 Cheetah（59-66%）之间。\n      3-seed variance ~±2%，与 Walker 相当。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole Swingup baseline v/e calibration (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, mean_eval, std_eval, mean_ve, std_ve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 290, 30, 0.11, 0.02]\n          - [35K, 385, 25, 0.22, 0.03]\n          - [55K, 573, 18, 0.38, 0.03]\n          - [105K, 718, 18, 0.60, 0.03]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole 3-seed baseline。收敛速度介于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cartpole baseline 建立了第三个 environment-specific v/e calibration point。\n      v/e asymptote 在 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间，为 3-environment 分析提供中间参考。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup trained dt_emb + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_051\"\n    description: \"Replicate delusional critic in Cartpole: dt=2 + subsample ON + trained dt_emb + H=8\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_25K: 175\n      seed0_eval_return_35K: 205\n      seed0_eval_return_45K: 190\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 140\n      seed0_normalized_ve_35K: 1.60\n      seed0_normalized_ve_45K: 1.85\n      seed0_normalized_ve_55K: 2.35\n      seed0_verdict: \"COLLAPSE_CONFIRMED\"\n      seed1_eval_return_35K: 215\n      seed1_eval_return_45K: 210\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 220\n      seed1_eval_return_105K: 310\n      seed1_normalized_ve_35K: 1.42\n      seed1_normalized_ve_45K: 1.58\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 1.35\n      seed1_normalized_ve_105K: 0.60\n      seed1_verdict: \"TRANSIENT_OVERESTIMATION_SELF_CORRECTION\"\n      seed2_eval_return_35K: 195\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 185\n      seed2_normalized_ve_35K: 1.48\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 1.45\n      seed2_verdict: \"DEGRADATION_BORDERLINE\"\n      cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 182\n      collapse_count: 1\n      nve_exceeds_1_5x_count: \"2/3 (seed 0 sustained, seed 1 transient; seed 2 stays 1.4-1.5x)\"\n      vs_baseline_pct_55K: \"-68%\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Cartpole 是 median 档的 \"cleaner cross-env replication\" 环境（vs Cheetah 的 borderline）。\n      机制：Cartpole Swingup 的 dynamics 包含强非线性区域（swingup phase 的大角速度变化\n      + near-top balancing 的 near-singularity），RSSM 在 dt=2 时对这些区域的预测误差显著。\n      特别是 reward prediction：Cartpole reward 与 pole angle cosine 强耦合，\n      dt=2 跳过 swingup 中间状态时 reward 预测偏差大，trained dt_emb 放大了这个偏差。\n      \n      Seed 0: sustained nve>1.5x（3 consecutive CKPTs: 1.60x@35K→1.85x@45K→2.35x@55K），\n      Walker-like accelerating pattern → collapse（eval 205→190→140）。\n      Seed 1: transient nve>1.5x（1.58x@45K），但 55K 回落至 1.35x → self-correction，\n      类似 Walker 的 009b 模式。Eval 最终恢复至 310@105K。\n      Seed 2: borderline（nve 1.42-1.48x，始终不达 1.5x），degradation 但无 clear pathology。\n      \n      Collapse rate: 1/3 = 33%，与 Walker 一致。Combined collapse prob = 2/6 = 33%（整体）。\n      含 Cheetah 0/3 后：2/9 = 22%，在 [0.15, 0.35] 内。\n      nve>1.5x 分类：Cartpole 2/3 正确（seed 2 是 boundary case）。\n      cross_env_mechanism_replication = 1（Cartpole clearly replicates, Cheetah does not）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole trained dt_emb (3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [step, seed0_eval, seed1_eval, seed2_eval, seed0_nve, seed1_nve, seed2_nve]\n        rows:\n          - [25K, 175, 180, 170, 1.45, 1.32, 1.35]\n          - [35K, 205, 215, 195, 1.60, 1.42, 1.48]\n          - [45K, 190, 210, 188, 1.85, 1.58, 1.45]\n          - [55K, 140, 220, 185, 2.35, 1.35, 1.45]\n          - [105K, \"collapsed\", 310, 175, \"—\", 0.60, 1.20]\n      - name: \"Cross-environment collapse summary\"\n        columns: [environment, seeds_tested, collapse_count, nve_gt_1_5x_count, mechanism_replicated]\n        rows:\n          - [Walker Walk, 3, 1, 2, \"✓ (clear)\"]\n          - [Cartpole Swingup, 3, 1, 2, \"✓ (clear)\"]\n          - [Cheetah Run, 3, 0, \"1 (borderline)\", \"✗ (degradation only)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole trained dt_emb 3-seed curves vs baseline。Seed 0 Walker-like collapse，seed 1 self-correction，seed 2 slow degradation。\"\n      - \"3-environment nve 对比：Walker 和 Cartpole 出现 >1.5x 加速 pattern，Cheetah 停留在 ~1.4x plateau。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cartpole 确认了 collapse 机制的跨环境泛化性——reward prediction 的 dt>1 偏差\n      在非 locomotion 环境中同样可被 trained dt_emb 放大为 delusional critic。\n      但仅 1/3 seeds collapse（与 Walker 相同），强化了 \"stochastic collapse\" 叙事。\n      Seed 2 的 borderline nve（1.45-1.48x）类似 Walker 009e 的预测——\n      trained dt_emb 并非在所有 seeds 中都能将 nve 推过 1.5x 阈值。\n      论文中 Cartpole 是 \"confirming cross-environment evidence\"，\n      Cheetah 是 \"boundary condition illustrating environment-dependent modulation\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cartpole Swingup dt_embed_dim=0 + subsample ON (3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_052\"\n    description: \"Causal control in Cartpole: dt=2 + subsample ON + dt_embed_dim=0 + H=8\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_eval_return_35K: 195\n      seed0_eval_return_55K: 210\n      seed0_normalized_ve_35K: 0.80\n      seed0_normalized_ve_55K: 0.72\n      seed1_eval_return_55K: 200\n      seed1_normalized_ve_55K: 0.78\n      seed2_eval_return_55K: 218\n      seed2_normalized_ve_55K: 0.70\n      cross_seed_mean_eval_55K: 209\n      cross_seed_mean_nve_55K: 0.73\n      vs_baseline_pct_55K: \"-64%\"\n      all_seeds_nve_below_1_5x: true\n      vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_eval: \"+27 (209 vs 182)\"\n      vs_trained_dtEmb_gap_nve: \"-0.70x (0.73 vs 1.43)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      移除 dt_embedding 在 Cartpole 中同样消除 elevated nve，pattern 与 Walker/Cheetah 一致。\n      3/3 seeds 的 nve 全程 <1.0x，无任何 overestimation。\n      Eval 退化（209 vs baseline 573@55K = -64%）主要来自 H=8 + subsample ON 的 learning signal deficit，\n      而非 value overestimation。\n      因果方向在 Cartpole 中与 Walker/Cheetah 完全一致：\n      有 dt_emb → nve>1.2x（Cartpole 均值 1.43x），无 dt_emb → nve<1.0x（均值 0.73x）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Cartpole causal comparison (mean across 3 seeds)\"\n        columns: [config, eval_55K, nve_55K, collapse]\n        rows:\n          - [\"trained dt_emb\", 182, 1.43, \"1/3 collapse\"]\n          - [\"dt_embed_dim=0\", 209, 0.73, \"no collapse\"]\n          - [\"baseline\", 573, \"1.0 (ref)\", \"N/A\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Cartpole dt_embed_dim=0 vs trained dt_emb——因果控制 pattern 与 Walker 定性一致。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cartpole 的因果控制实验确认了三环境一致性：\n      在所有 3 个 DMC 环境中，移除 dt_embedding → nve<1.0x → no collapse。\n      这是 C2 因果方向的最强跨环境证据。\n      即使 Cheetah 的 collapse mechanism 未清晰复现，\n      因果控制（dt_emb 有/无 → nve 升/降）在 3/3 环境中一致。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Analysis experiments\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"RSSM prediction quality: dt=1 vs dt=2 transitions\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_030\"\n    description: |\n      Measure RSSM reconstruction loss at dt=2 vs dt=1 across environments。\n      Walker 数据已有（exp_rssm_fidelity_analysis）。需扩展到 Cheetah + Cartpole。\n    expected_results:\n      walker_baseline_obs_dt1: 13.49\n      walker_baseline_obs_dt2: 27.50\n      walker_obs_gap: 2.04\n      walker_baseline_reward_dt1: 0.010\n      walker_baseline_reward_dt2: 0.016\n      walker_reward_gap: 1.56\n      cheetah_baseline_obs_dt1: 10.2\n      cheetah_baseline_obs_dt2: 16.8\n      cheetah_obs_gap: 1.65\n      cheetah_baseline_reward_dt1: 0.008\n      cheetah_baseline_reward_dt2: 0.011\n      cheetah_reward_gap: 1.38\n      cartpole_baseline_obs_dt1: 8.5\n      cartpole_baseline_obs_dt2: 18.2\n      cartpole_obs_gap: 2.14\n      cartpole_baseline_reward_dt1: 0.012\n      cartpole_baseline_reward_dt2: 0.022\n      cartpole_reward_gap: 1.83\n      cross_env_obs_gap_ordering: \"Cartpole(2.14) > Walker(2.04) > Cheetah(1.65)\"\n      cross_env_reward_gap_ordering: \"Cartpole(1.83) > Walker(1.56) > Cheetah(1.38)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      RSSM fidelity gap 的 environment dependence 是 median 档叙事的 mechanistic foundation。\n      Walker 数据已确认：obs gap 2.04x，reward gap 1.56x（real data）。\n      \n      Cheetah 预期最小的 gap（obs 1.65x, reward 1.38x）：\n      smooth locomotion dynamics + dense speed reward → dt=2 prediction 仅 moderately worse。\n      这直接解释了为什么 Cheetah 中 trained dt_emb 仅导致 mild degradation（nve ~1.4x）\n      而非 Walker/Cartpole 的 clear pathology（nve >1.5x）。\n      \n      Cartpole 预期最大的 gap（obs 2.14x, reward 1.83x）：\n      虽然 obs space 低维（5D → 低绝对误差），但 swingup 非线性导致 ratio 高。\n      Reward gap 1.83x 是 Cheetah 的 1.33 倍，反映 pole-angle-cosine reward 对 dt=2 误差的敏感性。\n      这解释了 Cartpole 作为第二个 \"clear replication\" 环境的地位。\n      \n      三点排序 Cartpole > Walker > Cheetah 恰好与 collapse severity 的排序一致：\n      Cartpole/Walker 有 clear nve>1.5x + collapse，Cheetah 仅 degradation。\n      但 3 个数据点不足以建立 quantitative 关系——论文中作 \"consistent with\" 而非 \"proves\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"RSSM fidelity gap: dt=1 vs dt=2 × environment (baseline models)\"\n        columns: [environment, obs_mse_dt1, obs_mse_dt2, obs_gap, reward_mae_dt1, reward_mae_dt2, reward_gap]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Walker Walk\", 13.49, 27.50, \"2.04x\", 0.010, 0.016, \"1.56x\"]\n          - [\"Cheetah Run\", 10.2, 16.8, \"1.65x\", 0.008, 0.011, \"1.38x\"]\n          - [\"Cartpole Swingup\", 8.5, 18.2, \"2.14x\", 0.012, 0.022, \"1.83x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: RSSM obs gap ratio 和 reward gap ratio × 3 environments。Cartpole > Walker > Cheetah。\"\n      - \"Scatter: RSSM reward gap ratio (x) vs mean nve peak in trained dt_emb config (y)。3 点近似线性。\"\n    analysis: |\n      plan_030 提供了 environment-dependent modulation 的 mechanistic evidence。\n      Cheetah 的低 RSSM gap → 低 nve → 无 collapse。Cartpole 的高 RSSM gap → 高 nve → 有 collapse。\n      这是论文的 Discussion 段核心论据之一，解释了为什么 \"same mechanism, different severity\"。\n      但仅 3 个环境点，quantitative relationship 只能是 suggestive。\n\n  - name: \"Actor entropy analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_031\"\n    description: \"Plot actor entropy vs training step for healthy vs collapsed Walker configurations\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_entropy_25K: 3.85\n      walker_008d_entropy_35K: 4.15\n      walker_008d_entropy_45K: 4.55\n      walker_008d_entropy_trend: \"increasing (actor confusion)\"\n      walker_006_entropy_35K: 3.95\n      walker_006_entropy_45K: 4.25\n      walker_006_entropy_55K: 5.30\n      walker_006_entropy_trend: \"sharply increasing\"\n      walker_008a_entropy_55K: 3.18\n      walker_008a_entropy_105K: 2.82\n      walker_008a_entropy_trend: \"stable to decreasing\"\n      walker_008f_entropy_55K: 3.42\n      walker_008f_entropy_trend: \"stable\"\n      walker_baseline_entropy_35K: 2.95\n      walker_baseline_entropy_105K: 2.48\n      walker_baseline_entropy_trend: \"decreasing (policy sharpening)\"\n      collapsed_vs_healthy_separation: \"clear after 25K\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Actor entropy 增高 = policy 变得更随机 = delusional critic gradient 的下游症状。\n      当 value function 高估 → actor 收到 misleading gradient →\n      policy 对不同 actions 的 preference 减弱 → entropy 升高。\n      \n      预期 collapsed configs（008d, 006）显示 entropy 单调上升：\n      008d 从 3.85@25K 升至 4.55@45K（actor 被 delusional critic 误导），\n      006 更极端（5.30@55K，对应其更严重的 collapse）。\n      \n      Healthy configs（008a, 008f, baseline）显示 entropy stable 或下降：\n      baseline 从 2.95@35K 降至 2.48@105K（policy sharpening，正常学习）。\n      008a 和 008f 介于两者之间但不上升。\n      \n      Median 档下 pattern 清晰但 noise 较大——entropy 是 high-variance metric，\n      个别 checkpoints 可能偏离趋势。但 collapsed vs healthy 的 qualitative 分离应在 25K+ 后明确。\n      这是 corroborating evidence 而非 primary evidence。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Actor entropy trajectories (Walker Walk)\"\n        columns: [config, entropy_25K, entropy_35K, entropy_45K, entropy_55K, trend]\n        rows:\n          - [\"baseline\", 3.15, 2.95, 2.85, 2.75, \"↓ decreasing\"]\n          - [\"008d (collapse)\", 3.85, 4.15, 4.55, \"—\", \"↑ increasing\"]\n          - [\"006 (collapse)\", 3.50, 3.95, 4.25, 5.30, \"↑↑ sharply\"]\n          - [\"008a (V-recovery)\", 3.28, 3.10, 3.02, 3.18, \"→ stable\"]\n          - [\"008f (stable)\", 3.38, 3.45, 3.32, \"—\", \"→ stable\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Actor entropy over training: collapsed configs diverge upward (red), healthy configs converge downward (blue)。25K 后 separation 明确。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Entropy analysis 在论文中作为 supplementary figure 或 appendix。\n      它不提供独立的 causal evidence，但 corroborates C2 的 causal diagram：\n      trained dt_emb → value overestimation → delusional critic gradient → actor confusion (↑ entropy) → performance collapse。\n      如果 collapsed configs 的 entropy 不上升，C2 chain 需修正。Median 档下预期 pattern 成立。\n\n  - name: \"Value prediction distribution vs realized returns\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_032\"\n    description: \"V(s) vs Monte Carlo return scatter plots for Walker configs\"\n    expected_results:\n      walker_008d_value_mc_correlation: 0.33\n      walker_008d_value_bias: \"+48% systematic overestimation\"\n      walker_008d_value_std_ratio: 2.15\n      walker_008a_value_mc_correlation: 0.70\n      walker_008a_value_bias: \"+9%\"\n      walker_008a_value_std_ratio: 1.22\n      walker_baseline_value_mc_correlation: 0.84\n      walker_baseline_value_bias: \"+5%\"\n      walker_baseline_value_std_ratio: 1.10\n      walker_008f_value_mc_correlation: 0.66\n      walker_008f_value_bias: \"+12%\"\n      walker_008f_value_std_ratio: 1.30\n    result_rationale: |\n      V(s) vs MC return 的联合分布将 v/e ratio proxy 升级为 rigorous value calibration 证据。\n      \n      008d（trained dt_emb, collapse）预期：\n      (a) systematic positive bias（值线远高于 y=x，+48%），\n      (b) 低 correlation（0.33，value 与 actual return 几乎 decouple），\n      (c) 高 variance ratio（2.15x，value 在不确定状态大幅波动）。\n      这三个特征共同构成 \"delusional critic\" 的 distributional fingerprint。\n      \n      008a/008f（healthy configs）预期接近 baseline（bias <12%, correlation >0.66）。\n      008f 的 correlation 略低（0.66 vs 0.70）可能反映 reward prediction 退化（reward_MAE=0.747）\n      引入的额外 noise，但不构成 delusional pattern。\n      \n      Median 档下 008d 的 low-correlation + high-bias pattern 应清晰可见，\n      但具体数值受 MC return 估计方法（N-step vs full episode）影响较大。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Value calibration summary (Walker Walk)\"\n        columns: [config, correlation, bias_pct, variance_ratio, verdict]\n        rows:\n          - [baseline, 0.84, \"+5%\", 1.10, calibrated]\n          - [\"008a (untrained)\", 0.70, \"+9%\", 1.22, mildly_optimistic]\n          - [\"008f (no dt_emb)\", 0.66, \"+12%\", 1.30, mildly_optimistic]\n          - [\"008d (trained)\", 0.33, \"+48%\", 2.15, delusional]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"2×2 scatter plot: V(s) vs MC return for baseline, 008a, 008f, 008d。008d 的点云远偏 y=x 线。\"\n      - \"Value error histogram (V-MC): 008d 明显右偏 heavy tail。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Distribution analysis 是 paper 中最有说服力的 supplementary evidence 之一。\n      008d 的 correlation=0.33 + bias=+48% 直接证明 \"delusional\"——\n      value function 对实际 return 的预测力极低且系统性偏高。\n      值得在 main text 给一个 figure（不仅是 appendix）。\n\n  - name: \"dt_embedding cosine similarity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_033\"\n    description: \"Analyze learned dt_embedding vectors: cosine similarity dt=1 vs dt=2 during training\"\n    expected_results:\n      cosine_sim_5K: 0.91\n      cosine_sim_15K: 0.74\n      cosine_sim_25K: 0.53\n      cosine_sim_35K: 0.40\n      cosine_sim_55K: 0.27\n      embedding_norm_dt1_35K: 1.18\n      embedding_norm_dt2_35K: 2.75\n      embedding_divergence_onset: \"~15K-25K (coincides with nve acceleration)\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Trained dt_embedding 在训练过程中逐步学会区分 dt=1 和 dt=2。\n      早期（<10K）两个 embedding 相似（cosine ~0.9），value function 尚未 exploit 差异。\n      15-25K 时 embedding 分离（cosine 降至 0.5-0.7），\n      恰好与 nve 开始加速的时间窗口吻合（008d@25K nve=1.78x）。\n      \n      dt=2 embedding 的 norm 增大（2.75 vs dt=1 的 1.18@35K）\n      表明 value function 放大了 dt=2 的表征——\n      可能因为 dt=2 transition 在 imagination 中产生更大的 \"value opportunity\"（实际上是虚假的）。\n      \n      Temporal correlation 提供了 mechanistic timeline：\n      embedding 分离 → value exploitation → nve>1.5x → collapse。\n      但 cosine similarity 下降的速率可能有 batch 间 noise，个别 checkpoint 偏离趋势。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"dt_embedding evolution during training (Walker 008d)\"\n        columns: [step, cosine_sim, norm_dt1, norm_dt2, nve_at_step]\n        rows:\n          - [5K, 0.91, 0.82, 0.88, \"~1.0x\"]\n          - [15K, 0.74, 0.98, 1.38, \"~1.2x\"]\n          - [25K, 0.53, 1.08, 2.10, \"~1.78x\"]\n          - [35K, 0.40, 1.18, 2.75, \"~1.71x\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-axis: cosine similarity (↓) and nve (↑) vs step。Divergence onset co-occurs at ~15-25K。\"\n      - \"2D PCA of dt_embedding at [5K, 15K, 25K, 35K]——dt=1 和 dt=2 clusters 逐步分离。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Cosine analysis 提供 mechanistic timeline。如果 embedding 分离与 nve 加速的时间吻合，\n      则 C2 的 mechanism story（dt_emb learning → value exploitation → collapse）\n      获得额外 temporal evidence 支持。P2 priority，但可做有说服力的 figure。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Mitigation pilot\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Uncertainty-gated imagination truncation pilot (Walker Walk, 1 seed)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_060\"\n    description: |\n      Monitor RSSM prediction uncertainty during imagination rollout;\n      truncate when exceeding threshold. Pilot on Walker Walk dt=2 + subsample ON.\n    expected_results:\n      implementation_status: \"partial — framework implemented but tuning incomplete by deadline\"\n      eval_return_55K: 320\n      eval_return_105K: 550\n      normalized_ve_55K: 1.15\n      normalized_ve_105K: 0.85\n      vs_baseline_105K: \"-40%\"\n      uncertainty_threshold_sensitivity: \"high — performance varies 30%+ across threshold values\"\n      verdict: \"INCONCLUSIVE — promising direction but threshold tuning insufficient\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Median 档核心假设：uncertainty-gated truncation 不在 deadline 前完成或结果 inconclusive。\n      \n      实现挑战：\n      1. RSSM 的 prediction uncertainty 没有现成的 well-calibrated 输出——\n         需要设计 uncertainty proxy（e.g., stochastic state 的 KL divergence，\n         或 reconstruction loss rolling average）。这本身需要 1-2 天实验。\n      2. 即使 proxy 可用，truncation threshold 是敏感超参——\n         太低则 imagination horizon 过短（回退到 dt=1 效果），\n         太高则不截断（回退到 dt=2 collapse 效果）。\n      3. Threshold 需要 per-environment 和 per-training-phase tuning，\n         进一步增加实验矩阵。\n      \n      预测：pilot 在 Walker Walk 上实现了 framework（能监测 uncertainty + 条件截断），\n      但 performance 高度依赖 threshold 值（30%+ variation），\n      最优 threshold 下达 ~60% baseline（550/916）——\n      优于 008d 的 collapse 但远低于 008e_v3 的 95%。\n      \n      Normalized v/e 从 1.15x@55K 降至 0.85x@105K——\n      truncation 确实减缓了 overestimation 但效果不如 008e_v3 的简单 dt=1 restriction。\n      \n      结论：方向正确但 tuning 需更多时间。论文中作为 Future Work 而非 main contribution。\n      C6 的 primary mitigation 仍是 008e_v3（dt=1 imagination, zero-cost）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Uncertainty-gated truncation vs alternatives\"\n        columns: [config, eval_105K, nve_105K, tuning_effort, verdict]\n        rows:\n          - [\"008e_v3 (dt=1 imag)\", \"870 (95%)\", 0.80, \"zero-cost\", \"recommended\"]\n          - [\"uncertainty-gated\", \"550 (60%)\", 0.85, \"high (threshold-sensitive)\", \"inconclusive\"]\n          - [\"008d (no mitigation)\", \"collapsed\", \">4.0x\", \"N/A\", \"failure\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Sensitivity plot: eval@105K vs uncertainty threshold value。U-shape with narrow optimal window。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Plan_060 的 inconclusive 结果实际上 strengthens C6 的 practical value：\n      即使更 sophisticated 的 uncertainty-gated 方案也难以匹配 008e_v3 的简单 dt=1 restriction。\n      论文中可以用一段讨论 \"why simple works better than smart in this case\"——\n      因为 RSSM 的 uncertainty 本身就是 poorly calibrated，\n      用它来 gate imagination 是 circular（用不可靠的 uncertainty 来判断何时不可靠）。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Stretch goals (P2)\n  # ============================================================\n\n  - name: \"Hopper Hop validation (3 seeds × 3 configs)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_040\"\n    description: \"Third locomotion DMC environment for generalization (P2, likely not completed before deadline)\"\n    expected_results:\n      completion_probability: \"30% (P2 priority, GPU budget tight)\"\n      baseline_asymptotic: 250\n      trained_dtEmb_peak: 115\n      trained_dtEmb_nve_peak: 1.55\n      trained_dtEmb_collapse_count: \"1/3 (partial)\"\n      no_dtEmb_eval_55K: 100\n      no_dtEmb_nve_55K: 0.88\n      baseline_ve_stable: \"55-62%\"\n    result_rationale: |\n      Hopper Hop 是高难度 DMC task（baseline ~250 远低于 Walker ~950）。\n      RSSM prediction quality 介于 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间\n      （hopping 有 contact events 但比 walking 更规律）。\n      \n      低 absolute performance + 高 noise → signal-to-noise ratio 差 →\n      结论 less conclusive，主要价值是提供 plan_030 scatter plot 的第四个点。\n      \n      P2 priority 意味着在 CoRL deadline 前大概率无法完成。\n      如果完成：trained dt_emb 的 nve 在 Walker 和 Cheetah 之间（~1.55x），\n      1/3 seeds collapse。因果控制（no dt_emb → stable）仍成立。\n      \n      论文即使没有 Hopper 也可成立（Walker + Cartpole + Cheetah 三环境已覆盖\n      locomotion + non-locomotion + high/low RSSM error spectrum）。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Hopper Hop results summary (if completed)\"\n        columns: [config, mean_eval_55K, mean_nve_55K, collapse_fraction]\n        rows:\n          - [baseline, 180, \"1.0 (ref)\", \"0/3\"]\n          - [trained dt_emb, 95, 1.55, \"1/3\"]\n          - [dt_embed_dim=0, 100, 0.88, \"0/3\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"4-environment RSSM gap vs peak nve scatter plot（如果 Hopper 完成提供第 4 个点）。\"\n    analysis: |\n      Hopper 在 median 档主要是 nice-to-have。论文核心已由 Walker + Cartpole + Cheetah 支撑。\n      如时间允许完成，额外一个数据点强化 environment-dependent modulation 的 empirical pattern。\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # Aggregated metrics consistency check\n  # ============================================================\n  # C6_recovery_pct_of_baseline: Walker seed 0 = 95%, seed 1 = 95%, seed 2 = 84% → range [84, 95], mean 91.4% ✓ [78, 93]\n  # nve_threshold_classification_accuracy: Walker 5/6 + Cheetah 4/6 + Cartpole 5/6 = 14/18 = 0.78 ✓ [0.7, 0.88]\n  # cross_env_mechanism_replication: 1 (Cartpole) ✓ [1, 1]\n  # collapse_prob_trained_dt_emb: Walker 1/3 + Cheetah 0/3 + Cartpole 1/3 = 2/9 = 0.22 ✓ [0.15, 0.35]\n  # walker_008e_v3_IQM_pct_baseline: ~90% ✓ [80, 92]\n  # walker_nve_separating_power: 5/6 = 0.833 ✓ [0.75, 0.9]\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b306baf1-2f33-45ae-aee8-039b275495d4","total_cost_usd":1.4224390000000002,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30888,"cache_read_input_tokens":122365,"output_tokens":39288,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30888,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":38873,"cache_read_input_tokens":68439,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":25204,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.025299000000000002,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":39288,"cacheReadInputTokens":122365,"cacheCreationInputTokens":56598,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.39714,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"65b580e1-f04b-423a-bf72-14f366380258"}
